<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Related Work</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Masked diffusion models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hoogeboom et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al., 2024</a>)</cite> extend continuous diffusion models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sohl-Dickstein et al., 2015</a>; <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2020</a>)</cite> to discrete data. Early work applied these models to specialized domains such as graph generation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vignac et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sun &amp; Yang, 2023</a>)</cite>, protein design <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gruver et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, and drug discovery <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, where non-sequential generation provides natural advantages. The field has evolved with recent commercial-scale language models like Gemini Diffusion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepMind, 2025</a>)</cite> and Mercury <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Labs et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, which demonstrate competitive performance on language generation, reasoning, and coding tasks. This suggests that MDMs can serve as viable alternatives to the autoregressive models that currently dominate LLMs. Against this background, this paper investigates the fundamental computational differences between generation paradigms and explores whether more powerful generation methods exist.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Several works have explored extensions to standard MDM through mechanisms that enable rewriting and editing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">von Rütte et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peng et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Havasi et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>, which relate to our any-process generation framework. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2025)</a></cite> introduces random remasking during inference, though this capability is not learned from data. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lou et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">von Rütte et al. (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sahoo et al. (2025)</a></cite> propose adding uniform noise in the forward process rather than using masks, with models learning to revert them in the backward process, but this approach generally underperforms since modifying tokens directly appears more difficult than unmasking. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peng et al. (2025)</a></cite> introduces path planning to control generation, though the planner is not trained end-to-end with the base model. Current with ours: <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Havasi et al. (2025)</a></cite> introduces edit operations to flow matching frameworks but faces similar limitations as uniform noise approaches; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2025a)</a></cite> introduces to insert tokens at any
position while <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025)</a></cite> proposes expansion
and delete, but these capabilities per se are
insufficient for handling hard reasoning tasks as
discussed in <a href="#S3" title="3 A Theory of Masked Diffusion ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Background: Masked Diffusion Model</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce the preliminaries of diffusion language models or masked diffusion models (MDM), following the notation established in <a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminary ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Let <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Sigma}=\Sigma\cup\{\textsf{M}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Sigma}=\Sigma\cup\{\textsf{M}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the extended vocabulary where <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">M</span> is the mask special token. Consider sequences <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}=(x_{t,1},x_{t,2},\ldots,x_{t,S})\in\bar{\Sigma}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>S</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}=(x_{t,1},x_{t,2},\ldots,x_{t,S})\in\bar{\Sigma}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> indexed by time <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum context length, <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of decoding steps, <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}=\{\textsf{M}\}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>S</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}=\{\textsf{M}\}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is the fully masked sequence and <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{T}\in\Sigma^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{T}\in\Sigma^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is the target clean sequence.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Forward Noising Process</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The forward noising process constructs training data by generating noisy versions <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> from clean sequences <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. Unlike the discrete inference steps in <a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminary ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, training uses continuous time <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math> with larger <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> denoting later denoising steps. MDM employs the <em id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">absorbing mask kernel</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al., 2021</a>)</cite> where the signal ratio <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=t/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=t/T</annotation></semantics></math> represents the marginal probability that a token remains unmasked. Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> increases monotonically with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{s}&lt;\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{s}&lt;\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;t</annotation></semantics></math>), later timesteps preserve more original tokens, consistent with our convention where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> is fully masked and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math> is clean. At each position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, tokens either stay unchanged or become <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">M</span>, and once masked, they “absorb” into this state. The marginal distribution is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q(x_{t,i}\mid x_{T,i})=\operatorname{Cat}(x_{t,i};\alpha_{t}\mathbf{e}_{x_{T,i}}+(1-\alpha_{t})\mathbf{e}_{\textsf{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Cat</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q(x_{t,i}\mid x_{T,i})=\operatorname{Cat}(x_{t,i};\alpha_{t}\mathbf{e}_{x_{T,i}}+(1-\alpha_{t})\mathbf{e}_{\textsf{M}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the one-hot vector for token <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\bar{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\bar{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>. To obtain noised sequence <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute the masking probability <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and mask each position independently with this probability.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training Objective</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reverse process aims to recover <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. MDM parameterizes <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{T}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{T}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> to predict the clean data directly (but as mentioned in <a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminary ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, many recent large-scale MDMs omit explicit timestep embeddings). For the absorbing mask kernel, the true posterior <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{x}_{s}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{x}_{s}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{x}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;t</annotation></semantics></math> has an analytical form. For each position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q(x_{s,i}\mid x_{t,i},x_{T,i})=\begin{cases}\text{Cat}(x_{s,i};\mathbf{e}_{x_{t,i}}),&amp;\text{if }x_{t,i}\neq\textsf{M}\\
\text{Cat}\left(x_{s,i};\frac{(1-\alpha_{s})\mathbf{e}_{\textsf{M}}+(\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s})\mathbf{e}_{x_{T,i}}}{1-\alpha_{s}}\right),&amp;\text{if }x_{t,i}=\textsf{M}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q(x_{s,i}\mid x_{t,i},x_{T,i})=\begin{cases}\text{Cat}(x_{s,i};\mathbf{e}_{x_{t,i}}),&amp;\text{if }x_{t,i}\neq\textsf{M}\\
\text{Cat}\left(x_{s,i};\frac{(1-\alpha_{s})\mathbf{e}_{\textsf{M}}+(\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s})\mathbf{e}_{x_{T,i}}}{1-\alpha_{s}}\right),&amp;\text{if }x_{t,i}=\textsf{M}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This means that, if position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is not masked at time <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, it remains unchanged at time <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>; if position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is masked at time <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, it transitions probabilistically between the original token and mask. The training objective is derived from the variational lower bound. For the absorbing mask kernel, it simplifies to:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,T),\mathbf{x}_{T}\sim p_{\text{data}},\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{T})}\left[-\frac{1}{|\{i:x_{t,i}=\textsf{M}\}|}\sum_{i:x_{t,i}=\textsf{M}}\log p_{\theta}(x_{T,i}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>CE</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{CE}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,T),\mathbf{x}_{T}\sim p_{\text{data}},\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim q(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{x}_{T})}\left[-\frac{1}{|\{i:x_{t,i}=\textsf{M}\}|}\sum_{i:x_{t,i}=\textsf{M}}\log p_{\theta}(x_{T,i}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t},t)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The loss is computed only on masked positions and averaged over the number of masked tokens, making this equivalent to conditional masked language modeling with proper normalization. Here, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled uniformly from the continuous interval <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math> during training, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled from the data distribution, and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by applying the forward noising process.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Methodological Details</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Model Architecture</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As described in <a href="#S4" title="4 Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, AP-MDM extends standard MDM with three additional capabilities: <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0F75FF;">remask</span> (rewrite via remasking), <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFB529;">insert</span> (insert masks), and <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B80000;">delete</span> (remove redundant masks). In principle, these capabilities can be implemented using a shared encoder-only Transformer backbone with three additional linear heads, adding minimal computational overhead.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Architecture</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <a href="#S4.E4" title="In 4.1 An Instantiation with unmask, remask, insert, and delete Operations ‣ 4 Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, AP-MDM uses four prediction heads on top of a shared encoder-only Transformer backbone. Given the hidden representation <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}_{t,i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}_{t,i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for position <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the heads output logits and probabilities:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta}(y_{t,i}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta}(y_{t,i}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{W}_{U}\mathbf{h}_{t,i}+\mathbf{b}_{U}),\quad\mathbf{W}_{U}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\Sigma|\times d}\quad\text{(unmask)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mtext>(unmask)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{W}_{U}\mathbf{h}_{t,i}+\mathbf{b}_{U}),\quad\mathbf{W}_{U}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\Sigma|\times d}\quad\text{(unmask)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{t,i}[1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{t,i}[1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(\mathbf{W}_{R}\mathbf{h}_{t,i}+b_{R}),\quad\mathbf{W}_{R}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times 1}\quad\text{(remask)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>(remask)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(\mathbf{W}_{R}\mathbf{h}_{t,i}+b_{R}),\quad\mathbf{W}_{R}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times 1}\quad\text{(remask)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{t,i}[2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{t,i}[2]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(\mathbf{W}_{I}\mathbf{h}_{t,i}+b_{I}),\quad\mathbf{W}_{I}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times 1}\quad\text{(insert)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>(insert)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(\mathbf{W}_{I}\mathbf{h}_{t,i}+b_{I}),\quad\mathbf{W}_{I}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times 1}\quad\text{(insert)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{t,i}[3]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{t,i}[3]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(\mathbf{W}_{D}\mathbf{h}_{t,i}+b_{D}),\quad\mathbf{W}_{D}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times 1}\quad\text{(delete)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>(delete)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(\mathbf{W}_{D}\mathbf{h}_{t,i}+b_{D}),\quad\mathbf{W}_{D}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times 1}\quad\text{(delete)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the unmask head outputs a probability distribution <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(y_{t,i}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(y_{t,i}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> over the vocabulary <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> for predicting tokens at masked positions, while the three control signal heads output binary probabilities for the corresponding operations. During inference, tokens are obtained via <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{t,i}=\argmax p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t,i}=\argmax p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and control signals are obtained by thresholding.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Self-Supervised Training</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In principle, one can design specialized loss functions corresponding to each operation, alongside the standard unmasking loss from MDM, by constructing self-supervised signals from the inherent structure of text data through augmentation strategies.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Unmasking Loss</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The unmasking loss would follow standard MDM training as described in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Background: Masked Diffusion Model ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>. For each training sample <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can sample <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,T)</annotation></semantics></math> and apply the forward masking process with signal ratio <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=t/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=t/T</annotation></semantics></math> to create <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t,i}=\begin{cases}x_{T,i}&amp;\text{with probability }\alpha_{t}\\
\textsf{M}&amp;\text{with probability }1-\alpha_{t}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>with probability </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>with probability </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t,i}=\begin{cases}x_{T,i}&amp;\text{with probability }\alpha_{t}\\
\textsf{M}&amp;\text{with probability }1-\alpha_{t}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The model would learn to predict original tokens at masked positions with time weighting:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.6,0.2,0.8}\textbf{unmask}}}=\mathbb{E}_{t,\mathbf{x}_{T},\mathbf{x}_{t}}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{i}m_{i}}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathbf{x}_{T}|}m_{i}\cdot\left(-\frac{\log p_{\theta}(x_{T,i}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t})}{t}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#9933CC;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#9933CC">unmask</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.6,0.2,0.8}\textbf{unmask}}}=\mathbb{E}_{t,\mathbf{x}_{T},\mathbf{x}_{t}}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{i}m_{i}}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathbf{x}_{T}|}m_{i}\cdot\left(-\frac{\log p_{\theta}(x_{T,i}\mid\mathbf{x}_{t})}{t}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> if position <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is valid (according to attention mask), 0 otherwise.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remasking Loss</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The remasking loss could train the model to identify incorrect tokens that should be remasked. For each sample <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can sample <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,T)</annotation></semantics></math> and create a corrupted sequence <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> using batch-internal shuffling (which effectively samples from the empirical token distribution rather than a biased uniform distribution):</p>
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{x}_{t,i}=\begin{cases}x_{T,i}&amp;\text{with probability }\alpha_{t}\\
\text{shuffled token}&amp;\text{with probability }1-\alpha_{t}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>with probability </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>shuffled token</mtext></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>with probability </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{x}_{t,i}=\begin{cases}x_{T,i}&amp;\text{with probability }\alpha_{t}\\
\text{shuffled token}&amp;\text{with probability }1-\alpha_{t}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The remasking labels are <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c_{t,i}[1]=\mathbf{1}[x_{T,i}\neq\tilde{x}_{t,i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t,i}[1]=\mathbf{1}[x_{T,i}\neq\tilde{x}_{t,i}]</annotation></semantics></math>, and the loss uses binary cross-entropy:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.06,0.46,1}\textbf{remask}}}=\mathbb{E}_{t,\mathbf{x}_{T},\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{t}}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{i}m_{i}}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathbf{x}_{T}|}m_{i}\cdot\text{BCE}(\text{logit}_{R,i},c_{t,i}[1])\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#0F75FF;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#0F75FF">remask</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>BCE</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>logit</mtext><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.06,0.46,1}\textbf{remask}}}=\mathbb{E}_{t,\mathbf{x}_{T},\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_{t}}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{i}m_{i}}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathbf{x}_{T}|}m_{i}\cdot\text{BCE}(\text{logit}_{R,i},c_{t,i}[1])\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates valid positions and BCE denotes binary cross-entropy with logits.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Insert Loss</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The insert loss could teach the model to identify positions where additional content is needed. For each sample <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can sample deletion probability <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and generate deletion indicators for each position <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. One would create the deflated sequence <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> by removing tokens at randomly selected positions. The insert labels would be <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t,j}[2]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t,j}[2]=1</annotation></semantics></math> for positions <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> that remain in <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> where the next position was deleted, 0 otherwise:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{1,0.71,0.16}\textbf{insert}}}=\mathbb{E}_{\delta,\mathbf{x}_{T},\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{j}m_{j}}\sum_{j=1}^{|\tilde{\mathbf{x}}|}m_{j}\cdot\text{BCE}(\text{logit}_{I,j},c_{t,j}[2])\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFB529;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#FFB529">insert</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>BCE</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>logit</mtext><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{1,0.71,0.16}\textbf{insert}}}=\mathbb{E}_{\delta,\mathbf{x}_{T},\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{j}m_{j}}\sum_{j=1}^{|\tilde{\mathbf{x}}|}m_{j}\cdot\text{BCE}(\text{logit}_{I,j},c_{t,j}[2])\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates valid positions in the deflated sequence.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Delete Loss</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The delete loss could train the model to distinguish between necessary and redundant mask tokens. One can use a two-step masking process: first apply standard MDM masking with <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=t/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=t/T</annotation></semantics></math> to create <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\text{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\text{base}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then sample insertion probability <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> to insert additional <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">M</span> tokens at randomly selected positions. The delete labels would distinguish mask origins:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{t,i}[3]=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }\hat{x}_{t,i}=\textsf{M}\text{ and inserted in step 2}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mtext> and inserted in step 2</mtext></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{t,i}[3]=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }\hat{x}_{t,i}=\textsf{M}\text{ and inserted in step 2}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The loss uses binary cross-entropy:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.72,0,0}\textbf{delete}}}=\mathbb{E}_{\gamma,\mathbf{x}_{T},\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{k}m_{k}}\sum_{k=1}^{|\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}|}m_{k}\cdot\text{BCE}(\text{logit}_{D,k},c_{t,k}[3])\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#B80000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#B80000">delete</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>BCE</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>logit</mtext><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.72,0,0}\textbf{delete}}}=\mathbb{E}_{\gamma,\mathbf{x}_{T},\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}}\left[\frac{1}{\sum_{k}m_{k}}\sum_{k=1}^{|\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{t}|}m_{k}\cdot\text{BCE}(\text{logit}_{D,k},c_{t,k}[3])\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates valid positions in the contracted sequence.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Combined Training Objective</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In principle, an AP-MDM training objective could balance all four capabilities:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{AP-MDM}}=\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.6,0.2,0.8}\textbf{unmask}}}+\lambda_{r}\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.06,0.46,1}\textbf{remask}}}+\lambda_{i}\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{1,0.71,0.16}\textbf{insert}}}+\lambda_{d}\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.72,0,0}\textbf{delete}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>AP-MDM</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#9933CC;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#9933CC">unmask</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#0F75FF;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#0F75FF">remask</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFB529;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#FFB529">insert</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#B80000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#B80000">delete</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{AP-MDM}}=\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.6,0.2,0.8}\textbf{unmask}}}+\lambda_{r}\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.06,0.46,1}\textbf{remask}}}+\lambda_{i}\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{1,0.71,0.16}\textbf{insert}}}+\lambda_{d}\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.72,0,0}\textbf{delete}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{r},\lambda_{i},\lambda_{d}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{r},\lambda_{i},\lambda_{d}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> are hyperparameters controlling the relative importance of each operation with default value <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Supervised Training</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to the self-supervised training approach described in <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Self-Supervised Training ‣ Appendix C Methodological Details ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
            
              §
            
          </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, AP-MDM can also be trained with explicit supervision when state-transition data is available. This applies to scenarios where we have access to the underlying generation process. It can also be combined with the self-supervised approach in <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Self-Supervised Training ‣ Appendix C Methodological Details ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
            
              §
            
          </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> for hybrid training, e.g. self-supervised in pretraining and supervised in finetuning.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data Format</h5>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each training sample consists of a state-transition tuple <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x}_{k},\mathbf{y}^{*},\mathbf{c}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x}_{k},\mathbf{y}^{*},\mathbf{c}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> where:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:15pt;">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{k}\in\bar{\Sigma}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{k}\in\bar{\Sigma}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>: current state (potentially containing <span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">M</span> tokens)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}^{*}\in\Sigma^{|\mathbf{x}_{k}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}^{*}\in\Sigma^{|\mathbf{x}_{k}|}</annotation></semantics></math>: target tokens for each position</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}^{*}=(c^{*}_{1},\ldots,c^{*}_{|\mathbf{x}_{k}|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}^{*}=(c^{*}_{1},\ldots,c^{*}_{|\mathbf{x}_{k}|})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{*}_{i}\in\mathcal{C}=\{0,1\}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{*}_{i}\in\mathcal{C}=\{0,1\}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>: ground-truth control signals</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Any-Process Generation with <span id="alg1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9933CC;">unmask</span>, <span id="alg1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0F75FF;">remask</span>, <span id="alg1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFB529;">insert</span>, and <span id="alg1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B80000;">delete</span> Operations</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.12" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
                
                
              Trained model <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, input prompt <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
                
                
              Generated sequence <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\text{final}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext>final</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\text{final}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
                
                
              <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}\leftarrow\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize with input prompt
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
                
                
              <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> stopping criterion not met <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{y}_{t},\mathbf{c}_{t})\leftarrow f_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{y}_{t},\mathbf{c}_{t})\leftarrow f_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Model forward pass
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}\leftarrow[]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}\leftarrow[]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize temporary sequence
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
                
                
                <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbf{x}_{t}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbf{x}_{t}|</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t,i}[3]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t,i}[3]=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t,i}=\textsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t,i}=\textsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg1.l9.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B80000;">delete</span> operation
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
                
                
                   <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">continue</span> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Skip this position
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Determine token value: Remask <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> Unmask <math id="alg1.l12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> Keep
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t,i}[1]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t,i}[1]=1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg1.l13.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l13.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0F75FF;">remask</span> operation
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
                
                
                   Append <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">M</span> to <math id="alg1.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg1.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span> <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t,i}=\textsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t,i}=\textsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg1.l15.5" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l15.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9933CC;">unmask</span> operation
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
                
                
                   Append <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg1.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else<span id="alg1.l17.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Keep unchanged
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
                
                
                   Append <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg1.l19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
                
                
                 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg1.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t,i}[2]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t,i}[2]=1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg1.l21.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l21.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFB529;">insert</span> operation
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
                
                
                   Append <span id="alg1.l22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">M</span> to <math id="alg1.l22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">23:</span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg1.l23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">24:</span>
                
                
                <span id="alg1.l24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">25:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t+1}\leftarrow\mathbf{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t+1}\leftarrow\mathbf{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">26:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow t+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">27:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l27.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">28:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training Objective</h5>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the state-transition data, the model learns to predict both the target tokens and control signals. The training objective consists of four components:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For positions where <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k,i}=\textsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k,i}=\textsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}_{i}\neq\textsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}_{i}\neq\textsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, predict the target token:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.6,0.2,0.8}\textbf{unmask}}}^{\text{sup}}=-\frac{1}{|\{i:x_{k,i}=\textsf{M},y^{*}_{i}\neq\textsf{M}\}|}\sum_{i:x_{k,i}=\textsf{M},y^{*}_{i}\neq\textsf{M}}\log p_{\theta}(y^{*}_{i}\mid\mathbf{x}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#9933CC;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#9933CC">unmask</mtext><mtext>sup</mtext></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.6,0.2,0.8}\textbf{unmask}}}^{\text{sup}}=-\frac{1}{|\{i:x_{k,i}=\textsf{M},y^{*}_{i}\neq\textsf{M}\}|}\sum_{i:x_{k,i}=\textsf{M},y^{*}_{i}\neq\textsf{M}}\log p_{\theta}(y^{*}_{i}\mid\mathbf{x}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For all valid positions, predict the control signals:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.06,0.46,1}\textbf{remask}}}^{\text{sup}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#0F75FF;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#0F75FF">remask</mtext><mtext>sup</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.06,0.46,1}\textbf{remask}}}^{\text{sup}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sum_{i}m_{i}}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathbf{x}_{k}|}m_{i}\cdot\text{BCE}(\text{logit}_{R,i},c^{*}_{i}[1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>BCE</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>logit</mtext><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sum_{i}m_{i}}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathbf{x}_{k}|}m_{i}\cdot\text{BCE}(\text{logit}_{R,i},c^{*}_{i}[1])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{1,0.71,0.16}\textbf{insert}}}^{\text{sup}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFB529;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#FFB529">insert</mtext><mtext>sup</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{1,0.71,0.16}\textbf{insert}}}^{\text{sup}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sum_{i}m_{i}}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathbf{x}_{k}|}m_{i}\cdot\text{BCE}(\text{logit}_{I,i},c^{*}_{i}[2])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>BCE</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>logit</mtext><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sum_{i}m_{i}}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathbf{x}_{k}|}m_{i}\cdot\text{BCE}(\text{logit}_{I,i},c^{*}_{i}[2])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.72,0,0}\textbf{delete}}}^{\text{sup}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#B80000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#B80000">delete</mtext><mtext>sup</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.72,0,0}\textbf{delete}}}^{\text{sup}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sum_{i}m_{i}}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathbf{x}_{k}|}m_{i}\cdot\text{BCE}(\text{logit}_{D,i},c^{*}_{i}[3])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>BCE</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>logit</mtext><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sum_{i}m_{i}}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathbf{x}_{k}|}m_{i}\cdot\text{BCE}(\text{logit}_{D,i},c^{*}_{i}[3])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates valid positions and BCE denotes binary cross-entropy with logits.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Combined Objective:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{AP-MDM}}^{\text{sup}}=\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.6,0.2,0.8}\textbf{unmask}}}^{\text{sup}}+\lambda_{r}\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.06,0.46,1}\textbf{remask}}}^{\text{sup}}+\lambda_{i}\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{1,0.71,0.16}\textbf{insert}}}^{\text{sup}}+\lambda_{d}\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.72,0,0}\textbf{delete}}}^{\text{sup}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>AP-MDM</mtext><mtext>sup</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#9933CC;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#9933CC">unmask</mtext><mtext>sup</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#0F75FF;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#0F75FF">remask</mtext><mtext>sup</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFB529;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#FFB529">insert</mtext><mtext>sup</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#B80000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#B80000">delete</mtext><mtext>sup</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{AP-MDM}}^{\text{sup}}=\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.6,0.2,0.8}\textbf{unmask}}}^{\text{sup}}+\lambda_{r}\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.06,0.46,1}\textbf{remask}}}^{\text{sup}}+\lambda_{i}\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{1,0.71,0.16}\textbf{insert}}}^{\text{sup}}+\lambda_{d}\mathcal{L}_{{\color[rgb]{0.72,0,0}\textbf{delete}}}^{\text{sup}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Inference-Time Algorithm</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As described in <a href="#S4" title="4 Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, AP-MDM generation follows an iterative process formulated as <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t+1}=g(f_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t+1}=g(f_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math>. We provide the complete inference-time sampling algorithm that implements the transition function <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> following <a href="#S4.E4" title="In 4.1 An Instantiation with unmask, remask, insert, and delete Operations ‣ 4 Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm implements the transition function <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{y}_{t},\mathbf{c}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{y}_{t},\mathbf{c}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in <a href="#S4.E4" title="In 4.1 An Instantiation with unmask, remask, insert, and delete Operations ‣ 4 Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Thresholds <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{r},\tau_{i},\tau_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{r},\tau_{i},\tau_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> control when operations are applied (default value <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> for all). The algorithm supports variable-length generation through dynamic insertion and deletion, and terminates when a stopping criterion is met (e.g., sequence convergence, generation of special tokens, or reaching a maximum iteration limit).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide implementation details for the experiments described in the main paper. All models are built on encoder-only Transformer architecture as described in <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Encoder Transformer Architecture ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>, with task-specific configurations detailed below.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model Architecture</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All models are based on encoder-only Transformer architecture with rotary positional embeddings (RoPE). For AP-MDM, we add three binary classification heads (remask, insert, delete) on top of the standard unmask head. We use no timestep embedding and set time conditioning to zero during supervised training. For Sudoku, we use 6 layers, 4 attention heads, hidden dimension <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=256</annotation></semantics></math>, feed-forward dimension <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4d=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4d=1024</annotation></semantics></math>, maximum sequence length 400, vocabulary size 31. For Parity, we use 1 layer, 1 attention head, hidden dimension <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=4</annotation></semantics></math>, feed-forward dimension <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4d=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4d=16</annotation></semantics></math>, maximum sequence length 3, vocabulary size 6, with approximately 200 total parameters. For Graph, we use 8 layers, 4 attention heads, hidden dimension <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=256</annotation></semantics></math>, feed-forward dimension <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4d=1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4d=1024</annotation></semantics></math>, maximum sequence length set to accommodate graphs of varying sizes, vocabulary size 55; the same configuration is used for the ARM baseline.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training Data Generation</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For supervised training as described in <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Supervised Training ‣ Appendix C Methodological Details ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
            
              §
            
          </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, training data consists of state-transition tuples <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x}_{k},\mathbf{y}^{*},\mathbf{c}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x}_{k},\mathbf{y}^{*},\mathbf{c}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> generated by simulating the natural solving or generation algorithms for each task. Starting from ground-truth target solutions, we execute task-specific algorithms and record the intermediate computation states at each step. For each state, we capture the current sequence <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> (with unknown or unfilled positions represented as <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">M</span>), the target values <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to be revealed, and the control decisions <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> indicating which operations (unmask, remask, insert, delete) should be applied. Concrete examples of data generation for Sudoku, Parity, and Graph tasks are provided in <a href="#A14" title="Appendix N Experiment: Sudoku Puzzle ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">N</span></a>, <a href="#A16" title="Appendix P Experiment: Parity ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">P</span></a>, and <a href="#A15" title="Appendix O Experiment: Graph Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">O</span></a>, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training Details</h5>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We train all models using AdamW optimizer with learning rate <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(0.9,0.999)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta_{1},\beta_{2})=(0.9,0.999)</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, and batch size 256. Learning rate follows a constant schedule with 250 warmup steps. We use mixed precision training (bfloat16) with gradient clipping at 1.0. Loss weights are set to <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{r}=\lambda_{i}=\lambda_{d}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{r}=\lambda_{i}=\lambda_{d}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> by default. Models are trained for up to 1M steps or until convergence. For Graph generation, we use 100K graph instances for training both AP-MDM and the ARM baseline. For Parity, we use only 4 training samples for AP-MDM, while the ARM baseline is trained with up to 10K instances.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Parallel Random Access Machine</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Random Access Machine (RAM) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arora &amp; Barak, 2009</a>)</cite> serves as the foundational theoretical model for sequential computation, featuring a single processor that can access any memory location in unit time regardless of address—hence “random access”, along with a finite set of registers and basic arithmetic/logical operations. This contrasts with models like Turing machines where memory access is sequential. The RAM’s key strength lies in its realistic abstraction of modern computers: it captures the essential computational primitives (arithmetic, memory access, conditional branching) while abstracting away hardware details, making it ideal for algorithm analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Parallel Random Access Machine (PRAM) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fortune &amp; Wyllie, 1978</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">JáJá, 1992</a>)</cite> extends this familiar RAM model to parallel computation by allowing <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)</annotation></semantics></math> processors to operate synchronously on shared memory with <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math>-bit word size. <span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          The <math id="footnote4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math>-bit word size choice ensures that pointer arithmetic, indexing, and basic integer operations on polynomially bounded values are unit-time, matching the standard RAM assumptions and avoiding artificial speedups due to unrealistically wide words.</span></span></span> Each processor in PRAM maintains its own program counter and unique identifier, enabling conditional branching and coordinated computation. The model operates in discrete synchronous time steps where all active processors execute simultaneously, inheriting RAM’s unit-cost random access property while adding the complexity of concurrent memory operations.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">PRAM Variants</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">PRAM has several variants, which differ in their memory access discipline, forming a hierarchy with precise complexity relationships. Let <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">EREW</span>, <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">CREW</span>, <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">CRCW<span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Common</span>, <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">CRCW<span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Arbitrary</span> and <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">CRCW<span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Priority</span> denote the classes of problems solvable in polynomial parallel time with polynomially many processors under each model, listed in order of increasing expressivity:</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold">EREW</span> (Exclusive Read, Exclusive Write): No concurrent access to any memory cell. Most restrictive but captures essential parallelism.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold">CREW</span> (Concurrent Read, Exclusive Write): Multiple processors may read the same cell simultaneously. Enables broadcast in <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> time vs. <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math> in EREW.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold">CRCW<span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Common</span>: Concurrent writes allowed only if all writers agree on the value. Boolean OR computable in <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> time.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold">CRCW<span id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Arbitrary</span>: Any concurrent writer may succeed; the choice is made arbitrarily (often modeled as random selection).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold">CRCW<span id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Priority</span>: Concurrent writes resolved by processor priority with various schemes (e.g., minimum/maximum index, sum of conflicting values).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Crucially, any algorithm in a stronger model can be simulated in a weaker model with at most <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math> parallel time overhead <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">JáJá, 1992</a>)</cite>. This polylogarithmic separation appears in basic primitives, broadcast requires <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math> rounds in <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">EREW</span> but <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> in <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">CREW</span>, yet the models remain polynomially equivalent for most complexity-theoretic purposes. <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">We adopt the <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">CREW</span> model throughout this paper</span>, where different processors are not allowed to write to the same memory cell simultaneously.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">PRAM, as an idealized abstraction of shared-memory multiprocessor systems, enables precise analysis of parallel algorithms and gives rise to parallel complexity classes such as <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">NC</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arora &amp; Barak, 2009</a>)</cite> (problems solvable in polylogarithmic parallel time using polynomially many processors). For example, PRAM can simulate algorithms on trees, linear arrays, meshes, and hypercubes without loss of parallel time, while reverse simulation costs at most <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\log^{2}P(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\log^{2}P(n))</annotation></semantics></math> overhead; Boolean circuits of depth <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> can be simulated on <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">CREW</span> in <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D)</annotation></semantics></math> time, making PRAM a natural model for measuring parallel time complexity in theory.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Below, we provide a more formal definition that will be used in proofs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Definition and Execution Process of Word-RAM</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We formalize the standard word-RAM that matches a single-processor PRAM (i.e., <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)=1</annotation></semantics></math>). Throughout, let the input length be <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and fix the word size <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(n)=\Theta(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(n)=\Theta(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Word Size, Universe, and Addresses.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the word universe be <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{U}=\{0,1,\dots,2^{w}-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕌</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{U}=\{0,1,\dots,2^{w}-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> with arithmetic modulo <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{w}</annotation></semantics></math>
(two’s-complement semantics). The address space is <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{0,1,\dots,S(n)-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{0,1,\dots,S(n)-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> for some
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(n)\leq n^{\mathcal{O}(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(n)\leq n^{\mathcal{O}(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Memory is a mapping <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:\mathcal{A}\to\mathbb{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝕌</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:\mathcal{A}\to\mathbb{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, <em id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">zero-initialized</em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(n)=\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(n)=\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> denote the address width. We adopt the transdichotomous condition:</p>
<table id="A5.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(n)\ \geq\ \max\{\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil,\ \lceil\log_{2}P(n)\rceil\}\qquad\text{and}\qquad w(n)=\Theta(\log n)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(n)\ \geq\ \max\{\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil,\ \lceil\log_{2}P(n)\rceil\}\qquad\text{and}\qquad w(n)=\Theta(\log n).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This ensures every address and processor ID fits in one word, enabling well-typed register-indirect addressing and processor identification.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Instruction Set and Semantics.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The machine operates with register names <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Reg}=\{0,1,\ldots,k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Reg}=\{0,1,\ldots,k\}</annotation></semantics></math> (for constant <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>), register file <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\in\mathbb{U}^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕌</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\in\mathbb{U}^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, immediate constants <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Imm}\subset\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖨𝗆𝗆</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Imm}\subset\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> (a fixed finite set independent of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>), and label identifiers <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Lab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖫𝖺𝖻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Lab}</annotation></semantics></math> for jump targets.<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              A label is a human-readable name for a program location (instruction index) serving as a jump/branch target.</span></span></span> We assume a constant-size register file with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathsf{Reg}|\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathsf{Reg}|\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> in the proof (any constant <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> suffices up to constant factors). Programs define a partial label table <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{addr}:\mathsf{Lab}\rightharpoonup\{0,\ldots,\ell\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>addr</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫𝖺𝖻</mi><mo stretchy="false">⇀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{addr}:\mathsf{Lab}\rightharpoonup\{0,\ldots,\ell\}</annotation></semantics></math> mapping each declared label to its instruction index (injective).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The instruction alphabet <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Instr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖨𝗇𝗌𝗍𝗋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Instr}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the following parameterized forms (<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,s\in\mathsf{Reg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,s\in\mathsf{Reg}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathsf{Imm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖨𝗆𝗆</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathsf{Imm}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\mathsf{Lab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖫𝖺𝖻</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\mathsf{Lab}</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A5.Ex1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex1X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{Instr}\;=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖨𝗇𝗌𝗍𝗋</mi><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{Instr}\;=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex1X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{\ \mathtt{LOAD}\ r,\,[s],\ \mathtt{STORE}\ [s],\,r,\ \mathtt{LOADI}\ r,\,c\ \}\" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝙻𝙾𝙰𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝚂𝚃𝙾𝚁𝙴</mi><mo lspace="0.500em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝙻𝙾𝙰𝙳𝙸</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{\ \mathtt{LOAD}\ r,\,[s],\ \mathtt{STORE}\ [s],\,r,\ \mathtt{LOADI}\ r,\,c\ \}\</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex1Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex1Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cup\ \{\ \mathtt{ADD}\ r,\,s,\ \mathtt{SUB}\ r,\,s,\ \mathtt{AND}\ r,\,s,\ \mathtt{XOR}\ r,\,s,\ \mathtt{SHL}\ r,\,s,\ \mathtt{SHR}\ r,\,s\ \}\" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∪</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝙰𝙳𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝚂𝚄𝙱</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝙰𝙽𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝚇𝙾𝚁</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝚂𝙷𝙻</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝚂𝙷𝚁</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cup\ \{\ \mathtt{ADD}\ r,\,s,\ \mathtt{SUB}\ r,\,s,\ \mathtt{AND}\ r,\,s,\ \mathtt{XOR}\ r,\,s,\ \mathtt{SHL}\ r,\,s,\ \mathtt{SHR}\ r,\,s\ \}\</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex1Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex1Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cup\ \{\ \mathtt{BRZ}\ r,\,L,\ \mathtt{JMP}\ L,\ \mathtt{HALT}\ \}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∪</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝙱𝚁𝚉</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝙹𝙼𝙿</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>𝙷𝙰𝙻𝚃</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cup\ \{\ \mathtt{BRZ}\ r,\,L,\ \mathtt{JMP}\ L,\ \mathtt{HALT}\ \}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Unbracketed registers <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,s</annotation></semantics></math> denote their word values <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r},R_{s}\in\mathbb{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕌</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r},R_{s}\in\mathbb{U}</annotation></semantics></math>. The bracketed form <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[s]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes register-indirect addressing: <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{LOAD }r,[s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">LOAD </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{LOAD }r,[s]</annotation></semantics></math> reads <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M[R_{s}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M[R_{s}]</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{STORE }[s],r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">STORE </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{STORE }[s],r</annotation></semantics></math> writes <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M[R_{s}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M[R_{s}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Bracketed operands are only allowed in <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{LOAD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙻𝙾𝙰𝙳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{LOAD}</annotation></semantics></math>/<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{STORE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚂𝚃𝙾𝚁𝙴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{STORE}</annotation></semantics></math>; nested or arithmetic addressing (e.g., <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[[s]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[[s]]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[r{+}c]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[r{+}c]</annotation></semantics></math>) is not part of this ISA. If <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{s}\notin\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{s}\notin\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, execution traps. Immediates are loaded as <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\bmod 2^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\bmod 2^{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The semantics of the instructions are as follows. We write <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\to\sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\to\sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for one execution step. Unless a jump changes it, set
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}\leftarrow\mathrm{pc}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}\leftarrow\mathrm{pc}+1</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}\in\{0,\ldots,\ell\}\cup\{\mathtt{HALT}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝙷𝙰𝙻𝚃</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}\in\{0,\ldots,\ell\}\cup\{\mathtt{HALT}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the program counter. Let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\oplus" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊕</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\oplus</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\wedge" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∧</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\wedge</annotation></semantics></math> denote bitwise XOR and AND;
let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ll" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≪</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ll</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gg" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≫</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gg</annotation></semantics></math> denote logical shifts; all arithmetic is modulo <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{LOAD}\ r,\,[s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝙻𝙾𝙰𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{LOAD}\ r,\,[s]</annotation></semantics></math>: 
<math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leftarrow R_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leftarrow R_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r}\leftarrow M[a]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r}\leftarrow M[a]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{STORE}\ [s],\,r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚂𝚃𝙾𝚁𝙴</mi><mo lspace="0.500em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{STORE}\ [s],\,r</annotation></semantics></math>: 
<math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leftarrow R_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leftarrow R_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M[a]\leftarrow R_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M[a]\leftarrow R_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{LOADI}\ r,\,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝙻𝙾𝙰𝙳𝙸</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{LOADI}\ r,\,c</annotation></semantics></math>: 
<math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r}\leftarrow c\bmod 2^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r}\leftarrow c\bmod 2^{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{ADD}\ r,\,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝙰𝙳𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{ADD}\ r,\,s</annotation></semantics></math> / <math id="A5.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{SUB}\ r,\,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚂𝚄𝙱</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{SUB}\ r,\,s</annotation></semantics></math>: 
<math id="A5.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r}\leftarrow(R_{r}\pm R_{s})\bmod 2^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>±</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r}\leftarrow(R_{r}\pm R_{s})\bmod 2^{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{AND}\ r,\,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝙰𝙽𝙳</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{AND}\ r,\,s</annotation></semantics></math> / <math id="A5.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{XOR}\ r,\,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚇𝙾𝚁</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{XOR}\ r,\,s</annotation></semantics></math>: 
<math id="A5.I2.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r}\leftarrow R_{r}\wedge R_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r}\leftarrow R_{r}\wedge R_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>   /   <math id="A5.I2.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r}\leftarrow R_{r}\oplus R_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r}\leftarrow R_{r}\oplus R_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{SHL}\ r,\,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚂𝙷𝙻</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{SHL}\ r,\,s</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A5.I2.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{SHR}\ r,\,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚂𝙷𝚁</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{SHR}\ r,\,s</annotation></semantics></math>: 
<math id="A5.I2.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leftarrow R_{s}\bmod w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>mod</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leftarrow R_{s}\bmod w</annotation></semantics></math>;   <math id="A5.I2.i6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{SHL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚂𝙷𝙻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{SHL}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A5.I2.i6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r}\leftarrow(R_{r}\ll h)\bmod 2^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r}\leftarrow(R_{r}\ll h)\bmod 2^{w}</annotation></semantics></math>; 
<math id="A5.I2.i6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{SHR}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚂𝙷𝚁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{SHR}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A5.I2.i6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r}\leftarrow\lfloor R_{r}/2^{h}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r}\leftarrow\lfloor R_{r}/2^{h}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> (logical right shift, zero fill).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{BRZ}\ r,\,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝙱𝚁𝚉</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{BRZ}\ r,\,L</annotation></semantics></math>: 
If <math id="A5.I2.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r}=0</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A5.I2.i7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}\leftarrow\mathrm{addr}(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>addr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}\leftarrow\mathrm{addr}(L)</annotation></semantics></math> else (no change to <math id="A5.I2.i7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>pc</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}</annotation></semantics></math> beyond <math id="A5.I2.i7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{JMP}\ L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙹𝙼𝙿</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{JMP}\ L</annotation></semantics></math>: 
<math id="A5.I2.i8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}\leftarrow\mathrm{addr}(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>addr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}\leftarrow\mathrm{addr}(L)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}\leftarrow\mathtt{HALT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝙷𝙰𝙻𝚃</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}\leftarrow\mathtt{HALT}</annotation></semantics></math> and execution stops.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{LOAD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙻𝙾𝙰𝙳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{LOAD}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{STORE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚂𝚃𝙾𝚁𝙴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{STORE}</annotation></semantics></math> handle memory access through register-indirect addressing, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{LOADI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙻𝙾𝙰𝙳𝙸</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{LOADI}</annotation></semantics></math> loads immediate constants, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{ADD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙰𝙳𝙳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{ADD}</annotation></semantics></math>/<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{SUB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚂𝚄𝙱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{SUB}</annotation></semantics></math> perform modular arithmetic, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{AND}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙰𝙽𝙳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{AND}</annotation></semantics></math>/<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{XOR}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚇𝙾𝚁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{XOR}</annotation></semantics></math> enable bitwise operations, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{SHL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚂𝙷𝙻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{SHL}</annotation></semantics></math>/<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{SHR}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚂𝙷𝚁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{SHR}</annotation></semantics></math> provide bit shifts. <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{BRZ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙱𝚁𝚉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{BRZ}</annotation></semantics></math> (branch
if zero) enables conditional branching, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{JMP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙹𝙼𝙿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{JMP}</annotation></semantics></math> provides unconditional jumps, and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{HALT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙷𝙰𝙻𝚃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{HALT}</annotation></semantics></math> terminates execution.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Programs and Configurations.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <em id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">program</em> is a pair <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=(I_{0},\ldots,I_{\ell},\mathrm{addr})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>addr</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=(I_{0},\ldots,I_{\ell},\mathrm{addr})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{i}\in\mathsf{Instr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖨𝗇𝗌𝗍𝗋</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{i}\in\mathsf{Instr}</annotation></semantics></math> and a partial label table <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{addr}:\mathsf{Lab}\rightharpoonup\{0,\ldots,\ell\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>addr</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝖫𝖺𝖻</mi><mo stretchy="false">⇀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{addr}:\mathsf{Lab}\rightharpoonup\{0,\ldots,\ell\}</annotation></semantics></math> mapping each declared label to its
instruction index (injective). The program is
<em id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">well formed</em> if whenever some <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{JMP}\ L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙹𝙼𝙿</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{JMP}\ L</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{BRZ}\ r,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝙱𝚁𝚉</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{BRZ}\ r,L</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\operatorname{dom}(\mathrm{addr})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>dom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>addr</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\operatorname{dom}(\mathrm{addr})</annotation></semantics></math>. Code is immutable during execution and independent of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> (and thus the RAM model considered here is uniform). A <em id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">configuration</em> is <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=(\mathrm{pc},R,M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>pc</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=(\mathrm{pc},R,M)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}\in\{0,\ldots,\ell\}\cup\{\mathtt{HALT}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝙷𝙰𝙻𝚃</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}\in\{0,\ldots,\ell\}\cup\{\mathtt{HALT}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the program counter, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\in\mathbb{U}^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕌</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\in\mathbb{U}^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the register file, and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:\mathcal{A}\to\mathbb{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝕌</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:\mathcal{A}\to\mathbb{U}</annotation></semantics></math> is memory. Input occupies <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M[0..n-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M[0..n-1]</annotation></semantics></math>; output is read from a designated location upon termination.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Initialization.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given an input instance of length <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, initialization proceeds as follows:</p>
<ol id="A5.I3" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A5.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Build the label table <math id="A5.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{addr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>addr</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{addr}</annotation></semantics></math> from the loaded code and check well-formedness (every label operand in the code must appear exactly once as a declared label).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Zero-initialize memory <math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and write the input into a designated block (e.g., <math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M[0..n-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M[0..n-1]</annotation></semantics></math>) using the agreed-upon encoding.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Set all registers to zero: <math id="A5.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,\ldots,k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,\ldots,k\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Set the program counter to the first instruction: <math id="A5.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The choice <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\geq\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\geq\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> ensures that register-indirect addressing is well-typed: a bracketed operand <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[s]</annotation></semantics></math> uses <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> as an address in <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Execution Cycle.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}\neq\mathtt{HALT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝙷𝙰𝙻𝚃</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}\neq\mathtt{HALT}</annotation></semantics></math> and no trap occurs, the machine advances in discrete steps. Each successful step costs one time unit. Let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{pc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>pc</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{pc}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the instruction at index <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>pc</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each step follows the fetch-decode-execute-commit cycle:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A5.I4" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A5.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fetch</span>: Read the current instruction <math id="A5.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\leftarrow I_{\mathrm{pc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>pc</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\leftarrow I_{\mathrm{pc}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A5.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}\notin\{0,\ldots,\ell\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}\notin\{0,\ldots,\ell\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the run is invalid and we define this as a trap.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Decode and read operands</span>: Parse the opcode and operands of <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> without changing the machine state. Unbracketed registers <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,s</annotation></semantics></math> denote their current word values <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{r},R_{s}\in\mathbb{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕌</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{r},R_{s}\in\mathbb{U}</annotation></semantics></math> (used as data). A bracketed operand <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[s]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the candidate address <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leftarrow R_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leftarrow R_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. An immediate <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathsf{Imm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖨𝗆𝗆</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathsf{Imm}</annotation></semantics></math> is interpreted as <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\bmod 2^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\bmod 2^{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. A label <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> resolves to <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{addr}(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>addr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{addr}(L)</annotation></semantics></math> (guaranteed by well-formedness). No writes occur in this phase.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A5.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Execute</span>: Apply the instruction semantics of <math id="A5.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> to compute a finite <em id="A5.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">write-set</em> <math id="A5.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> (register and/or memory locations with their new values) and the <em id="A5.I4.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">next program counter</em> <math id="A5.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}_{\text{next}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>pc</mi><mtext>next</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}_{\text{next}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For memory-referencing instructions, a bracketed operand <math id="A5.I4.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[s]</annotation></semantics></math> is valid only if <math id="A5.I4.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=R_{s}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=R_{s}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise a trap occurs. By default <math id="A5.I4.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}_{\text{next}}=\mathrm{pc}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>pc</mi><mtext>next</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}_{\text{next}}=\mathrm{pc}+1</annotation></semantics></math>, except for jumps/branches/halting which set it to <math id="A5.I4.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{addr}(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>addr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{addr}(L)</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="A5.I4.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{HALT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙷𝙰𝙻𝚃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{HALT}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A5.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Commit (writeback)</span>: Atomically apply the writes in <math id="A5.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.I4.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R,M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R,M)</annotation></semantics></math> and then set <math id="A5.I4.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}\leftarrow\mathrm{pc}_{\text{next}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>pc</mi><mtext>next</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}\leftarrow\mathrm{pc}_{\text{next}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Atomicity means all effects of the step become visible only at the end of the step.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A5.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cost and continuation</span>: If no trap occurred, charge one unit of time for this step and proceed to the next; otherwise the run aborts (abnormal termination), and only successfully committed steps are counted.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Termination and Complexity.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Execution halts when <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}=\mathtt{HALT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝙷𝙰𝙻𝚃</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}=\mathtt{HALT}</annotation></semantics></math>. The algorithm’s output is read from the designated output location(s) in memory (or registers) as specified by the program. Under the assumptions above and for well-formed programs with legal memory accesses, the step relation is deterministic and yields a unique next state at each iteration. The <em id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">time complexity</em> of an algorithm is the number of executed instructions before halting. A <em id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">trap</em> aborts the run immediately (abnormal termination); only successfully committed steps are counted in time.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The RAM model defined here is polynomially equivalent to
bit-complexity RAM (a <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math> factor separates their running times) and to richer word-RAMs
that add <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{MUL}/\mathtt{DIV}/\mathtt{POPCNT}/\mathtt{CLZ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝙼𝚄𝙻</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>𝙳𝙸𝚅</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>𝙿𝙾𝙿𝙲𝙽𝚃</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>𝙲𝙻𝚉</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{MUL}/\mathtt{DIV}/\mathtt{POPCNT}/\mathtt{CLZ}</annotation></semantics></math> (whose presence typically improves
only by constant or <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\log n</annotation></semantics></math> factors).</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Single-Processor Execution (Word-RAM semantics with PID init)</figcaption>
<p id="alg2.4" class="ltx_p ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom"><em id="alg2.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Note.</em> In PRAM, <math id="alg2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{STORE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚂𝚃𝙾𝚁𝙴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{STORE}</annotation></semantics></math> generates a pending write committed at the end of the round under the <span id="alg2.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">CREW</span> rule. In the single-processor case, the store can be applied immediately.</p>
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<div id="alg2.5" class="ltx_listing ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
                
                
              Program <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=(I_{0},\dots,I_{\ell},\mathrm{addr})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>addr</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=(I_{0},\dots,I_{\ell},\mathrm{addr})</annotation></semantics></math>, shared memory <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:\mathcal{A}\!\to\!\mathbb{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝕌</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:\mathcal{A}\!\to\!\mathbb{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, word size <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, processor id <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{pid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗉𝗂𝖽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{pid}</annotation></semantics></math>, processor budget <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)</annotation></semantics></math> (optional)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Init:</span> <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pc\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pc\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R[j]\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R[j]\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg2.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="alg2.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R[0]\leftarrow\mathsf{pid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝗉𝗂𝖽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R[0]\leftarrow\mathsf{pid}</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">optional: <math id="alg2.l2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R[1]\leftarrow P(n)\bmod 2^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R[1]\leftarrow P(n)\bmod 2^{w}</annotation></semantics></math></span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pc\neq\mathtt{HALT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝙷𝙰𝙻𝚃</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pc\neq\mathtt{HALT}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\leftarrow I_{pc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\leftarrow I_{pc}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l4.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> fetch
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pc_{\text{next}}\leftarrow pc+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>next</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pc_{\text{next}}\leftarrow pc+1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> default fall-through
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
                
                
                <span id="alg2.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LOAD</span> <math id="alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,[s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,[s]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg2.l6.5" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> decode
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leftarrow R[s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leftarrow R[s]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\notin\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\notin\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
                
                
                   <span id="alg2.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">trap</span> 
</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg2.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R[r]\leftarrow M[a]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R[r]\leftarrow M[a]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l11.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> execute
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
                
                
