                <span id="alg2.l40.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span> <span id="alg2.l40.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="alg2.l40.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">HALT </span> <span id="alg2.l40.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l41" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">41:</span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg2.l41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pc_{\text{next}}\leftarrow\mathtt{HALT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>next</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝙷𝙰𝙻𝚃</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pc_{\text{next}}\leftarrow\mathtt{HALT}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l42" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">42:</span>
                
                
                <span id="alg2.l42.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l43" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">43:</span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg2.l43.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">trap</span> <span id="alg2.l43.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> unknown opcode or malformed operands
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l44" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">44:</span>
                
                
                <span id="alg2.l44.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l44.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l45" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">45:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pc\leftarrow pc_{\text{next}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>next</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pc\leftarrow pc_{\text{next}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l45.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> commit PC; regs/memory updated in each branch above
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l46" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">46:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l46.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l46.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Extension to CREW PRAM</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We extend the Word-RAM defined above to a parallel machine with a processor-budget function <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> (typically <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)\leq n^{\mathcal{O}(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)\leq n^{\mathcal{O}(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>). All word-size/address-width assumptions, the instruction alphabet <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Instr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖨𝗇𝗌𝗍𝗋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Instr}</annotation></semantics></math>, the immediate-set restriction, and the <em id="A5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">single-processor</em> instruction semantics are exactly as in the Word-RAM subsection.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Processors and Shared State.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Processors are indexed by <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,\ldots,P(n)-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,\ldots,P(n)-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each processor has its own program counter and register file; memory is shared:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\;=\;\bigl((\mathrm{pc}_{0},\ldots,\mathrm{pc}_{P(n)-1}),\ (R^{0},\ldots,R^{P(n)-1}),\ M\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>pc</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>pc</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\;=\;\bigl((\mathrm{pc}_{0},\ldots,\mathrm{pc}_{P(n)-1}),\ (R^{0},\ldots,R^{P(n)-1}),\ M\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}_{i}\in\{0,\ldots,\ell\}\cup\{\mathtt{HALT}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>pc</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝙷𝙰𝙻𝚃</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}_{i}\in\{0,\ldots,\ell\}\cup\{\mathtt{HALT}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{i}=(R^{i}_{0},\ldots,R^{i}_{k})\in\mathbb{U}^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕌</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{i}=(R^{i}_{0},\ldots,R^{i}_{k})\in\mathbb{U}^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. All processors run the same program <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=(I_{0},\ldots,I_{\ell},\mathrm{addr})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>addr</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=(I_{0},\ldots,I_{\ell},\mathrm{addr})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Initialization (with Processor IDs).</h5>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At time <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ol id="A5.I5" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A5.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Build <math id="A5.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{addr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>addr</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{addr}</annotation></semantics></math> and check well-formedness (as in Word-RAM); zero-initialize <math id="A5.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and write the input block.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A5.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,\ldots,P(n)-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,\ldots,P(n)-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="A5.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}_{i}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>pc</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}_{i}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> and clear registers; then write <em id="A5.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">processor-local identifiers:</em> <span id="A5.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline"><math id="A5.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{i}_{0}\leftarrow i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{i}_{0}\leftarrow i</annotation></semantics></math></span> and, if <math id="A5.I5.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)\leq 2^{w(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)\leq 2^{w(n)}</annotation></semantics></math>, optionally <span id="A5.I5.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_underline"><math id="A5.I5.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{i}_{1}\leftarrow P(n)\bmod 2^{w(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>mod</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{i}_{1}\leftarrow P(n)\bmod 2^{w(n)}</annotation></semantics></math></span>. All other <math id="A5.I5.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{i}_{j}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{i}_{j}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">These two words are provided so that processors can branch, partition work, and self-disable if unused.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Concurrent-Access Policy (CREW).</h5>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Multiple processors may <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">read</em> the same address in the same round; <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">writes must be exclusive</em>: if two or more writes target the same address in a round, the run traps (abnormal termination).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Round Semantics (Referencing the Word-RAM Step).</h5>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each active processor executes exactly one instruction using the single-processor Word-RAM step semantics; the only new aspects are (i) simultaneous execution by many processors and (ii) end-of-round memory commit subject to the <span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">CREW</span> policy. Execution proceeds in synchronous rounds <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,1,2,\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,1,2,\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> with state <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t}=((\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t})_{i},(R^{i,t})_{i},M^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>pc</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t}=((\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t})_{i},(R^{i,t})_{i},M^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. In round <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, each active processor <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t}\in\{0,\ldots,\ell\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>pc</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t}\in\{0,\ldots,\ell\}</annotation></semantics></math> executes instruction <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><msubsup><mi>pc</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> on its local snapshot <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathrm{pc}=\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t},\ R=R^{i,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>pc</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>pc</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathrm{pc}=\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t},\ R=R^{i,t})</annotation></semantics></math> and shared memory <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. After all processors compute their local effects, the round commits: register writebacks <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{i,t}\to R^{i,t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{i,t}\to R^{i,t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> (independently), then memory writes to <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> under <span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">CREW</span> constraints, finally program counter updates <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>pc</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Termination and Cost Measures.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The parallel run terminates when <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t}=\mathtt{HALT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>pc</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝙷𝙰𝙻𝚃</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t}=\mathtt{HALT}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> (or traps on an invalid access/conflict). One round costs one unit of <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">parallel time</em>. The <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">work</em> is the total number of executed instructions <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(n)=\sum_{t}|\{\,i:\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t}\in\{0,\ldots,\ell\}\,\}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>pc</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(n)=\sum_{t}|\{\,i:\mathrm{pc}_{i}^{t}\in\{0,\ldots,\ell\}\,\}|</annotation></semantics></math>, and the <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">span</em> is <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\infty}(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\infty}(n)</annotation></semantics></math> (the critical-path length). For <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)</annotation></semantics></math> processors the Brent bound holds <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">JáJá, 1992</a>)</cite>:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{P(n)}(n)\ \leq\ \Big\lceil\frac{W(n)}{P(n)}\Big\rceil+T_{\infty}(n)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{P(n)}(n)\ \leq\ \Big\lceil\frac{W(n)}{P(n)}\Big\rceil+T_{\infty}(n).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A single-processor run (<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)=1</annotation></semantics></math>) coincides with the Word-RAM model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remarks (on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)</annotation></semantics></math>, Processor IDs, and Unused Processors).</h5>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(1) <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Uniformity:</em> the code <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and the immediate set <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Imm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖨𝗆𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Imm}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>; only the hardware parameters <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(n)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(n)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)</annotation></semantics></math> scale with input size. (2) <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Processor IDs:</em> the values <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)</annotation></semantics></math> are provided via initialization registers (<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{i}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{i}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and optionally <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{i}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{i}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) for branching and work partitioning; programs may copy/overwrite them. (3) <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Unused processors:</em> if an algorithm needs only <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(n)\leq P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(n)\leq P(n)</annotation></semantics></math> processors, each processor executes a short self-filter based on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., <span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">if <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq m(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq m(n)</annotation></semantics></math> then HALT</span>), or computes its assigned block; processors with empty assignment halt in <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> rounds, which does not affect the asymptotic parallel time.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm for a single-processor in PRAM is shown in <a href="#alg2" title="In Termination and Complexity. ‣ E.1 Definition and Execution Process of Word-RAM ‣ Appendix E Parallel Random Access Machine ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Encoder Transformer Architecture</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section presents encoder-only Transformers, which form the backbone of MDM. We will first establish the sequence-wise extension operation, then define the core components, including bidirectional self-attention, multi-head mechanisms, and feed-forward layers, before assembling the complete architecture.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We consider an encoder-only Transformer with <math id="A6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> heads, <math id="A6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers, hidden size <math id="A6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, and feed-forward width <math id="A6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>. We will use the following notations:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Position-Indexed Seq-to-Embedding Function)<span id="Thmdefinition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a set <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(B)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of all functions <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> such that for every sequence <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})\in\Sigma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})\in\Sigma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and every index <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, the value <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(x,i)\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(x,i)\in B</annotation></semantics></math> is defined. We write this succinctly as</span></p>
<table id="A6.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:(\Sigma^{*},\mathbb{N})\to B." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:(\Sigma^{*},\mathbb{N})\to B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and call this <em id="Thmdefinition4.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">position-indexed seq-to-embedding function</em>. We also define <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}=\cup_{d\in\mathbb{N}^{+}}\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em">∪</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=\cup_{d\in\mathbb{N}^{+}}\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> as the union of all such classes across real spaces of all output dimensions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Canonical Extension to Seq-to-Seq Function)<span id="Thmdefinition5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a position-indexed seq-to-embedding function <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in\mathcal{H}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in\mathcal{H}(B)</annotation></semantics></math>, its <em id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">canonical extension</em> is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A6.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\psi}:\Sigma^{*}\to B^{*}\quad\text{where}\quad[\overline{\psi}(x)]_{i}=\psi(x,i)\qquad(i\in[|x|])." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\psi}:\Sigma^{*}\to B^{*}\quad\text{where}\quad[\overline{\psi}(x)]_{i}=\psi(x,i)\qquad(i\in[|x|]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For elementwise functions <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{g}:(\mathbb{R}^{d})^{*}\to(\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}})^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{g}:(\mathbb{R}^{d})^{*}\to(\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}})^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\overline{g}(h_{1:n})]_{i}=g(h_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\overline{g}(h_{1:n})]_{i}=g(h_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a special case where <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi(h_{1:n},i)=g(h_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(h_{1:n},i)=g(h_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> (ignoring cross-position context). When the arity is clear, we reuse the bar notation for both position-indexed and elementwise extensions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now define the individual components of encoder Transformers:</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bidirectional Self-Attention.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The key difference from decoder Transformers is bidirectional attention, where each position can attend to all positions in the sequence. Let <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> be the head dimension. For <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q},W_{K},W_{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{h}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q},W_{K},W_{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{h}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{O}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{O}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define single-head attention on sequence of embeddings <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{1:n}\in(\mathbb{R}^{d})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1:n}\in(\mathbb{R}^{d})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{Q}h_{i},\quad k_{j}=W_{K}h_{j},\quad v_{j}=W_{V}h_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{Q}h_{i},\quad k_{j}=W_{K}h_{j},\quad v_{j}=W_{V}h_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle[\mathrm{SA}_{\theta}(h_{1:n})]_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>SA</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[\mathrm{SA}_{\theta}(h_{1:n})]_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{O}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\alpha_{ij}v_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{O}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\alpha_{ij}v_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,\cdot}=\mathrm{softmax}\big((q_{i}^{\top}k_{j})_{j=1}^{n}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,\cdot}=\mathrm{softmax}\big((q_{i}^{\top}k_{j})_{j=1}^{n}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=(W_{Q},W_{K},W_{V},W_{O})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=(W_{Q},W_{K},W_{V},W_{O})</annotation></semantics></math>. Position <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> attends to all <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> without causal restrictions. We use standard <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\sqrt{d_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\sqrt{d_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> scaling.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multi-Head Attention.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathrm{MHA}}=(\theta^{(1)},\ldots,\theta^{(H)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>MHA</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathrm{MHA}}=(\theta^{(1)},\ldots,\theta^{(H)})</annotation></semantics></math>, we combine heads via summation:</p>
<table id="A6.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\mathrm{MHA}_{\theta_{\mathrm{MHA}}}(h_{1:n})]_{i}=\sum_{t=1}^{H}[\mathrm{SA}_{\theta^{(t)}}(h_{1:n})]_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>MHA</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>MHA</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>SA</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathrm{MHA}_{\theta_{\mathrm{MHA}}}(h_{1:n})]_{i}=\sum_{t=1}^{H}[\mathrm{SA}_{\theta^{(t)}}(h_{1:n})]_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that this differs from practical implementations which concatenate heads with dimension <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d/H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d/H</annotation></semantics></math> each, but maintains equivalent theoretical expressivity.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Feed-Forward and Projection.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=d_{\mathrm{FF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>FF</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=d_{\mathrm{FF}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{w\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{w\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times w}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FF}_{\theta}(h)=W_{2}\,\sigma(W_{1}h)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>FF</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FF}_{\theta}(h)=W_{2}\,\sigma(W_{1}h)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For output projection, <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PROJ}_{\vartheta}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{|\Sigma|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>PROJ</mi><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PROJ}_{\vartheta}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{|\Sigma|}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PROJ}_{\vartheta}(h)=\vartheta h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>PROJ</mi><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PROJ}_{\vartheta}(h)=\vartheta h</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta\in\mathbb{R}^{|\Sigma|\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta\in\mathbb{R}^{|\Sigma|\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. We apply these via sequence-wise extension: <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathrm{FF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>FF</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathrm{FF}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathrm{PROJ}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>PROJ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathrm{PROJ}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For AP-MDM as described in <a href="#S4" title="4 Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, besides the above heads for <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9933CC;">unmask</span>, it would require three additional binary classification heads on top of the final layer: <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PROJ}_{R}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>PROJ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PROJ}_{R}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0F75FF;">remask</span>, <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PROJ}_{I}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>PROJ</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PROJ}_{I}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFB529;">insert</span>, and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PROJ}_{D}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>PROJ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PROJ}_{D}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B80000;">delete</span> operations, each followed by sigmoid activation. Therefore, <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PROJ}_{\vartheta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>PROJ</mi><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PROJ}_{\vartheta}</annotation></semantics></math> is a mapping from <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{|\Sigma|+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{|\Sigma|+3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Embeddings.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define token embedding <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TE}:\Sigma\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TE}:\Sigma\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and positional embedding <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PE}:\mathbb{N}^{+}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>PE</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PE}:\mathbb{N}^{+}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (which can be flexibly chosen and will be specified when used). Combined as <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathrm{TE}}+\overline{\mathrm{PE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>TE</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>PE</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathrm{TE}}+\overline{\mathrm{PE}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We write <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TE},\mathrm{PE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>PE</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TE},\mathrm{PE}</annotation></semantics></math> for their sequence-wise extensions when clear from context.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Residual Connections.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The identity function <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Id}_{d}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Id}_{d}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Id}_{d}(x)=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Id}_{d}(x)=x</annotation></semantics></math>. A <em id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">residual connection</em> is defined as <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f+\mathrm{Id}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f+\mathrm{Id}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Id}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Id}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity function.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we assemble these components into the encoder transformer architecture:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Encoder Transformer layer)<span id="Thmdefinition6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">An encoder layer is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A6.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{EncTF}_{\mathrm{MHA},\mathrm{FF}}=(\overline{\mathrm{FF}_{\mathrm{FF}}}+\overline{\mathrm{Id}_{d}})\circ(\mathrm{MHA}_{\theta_{\mathrm{MHA}}}+\overline{\mathrm{Id}_{d}}):(\mathbb{R}^{d})^{*}\to(\mathbb{R}^{d})^{*}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>EncTF</mi><mrow><mi>MHA</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>FF</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>FF</mi><mi>FF</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>MHA</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>MHA</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{EncTF}_{\mathrm{MHA},\mathrm{FF}}=(\overline{\mathrm{FF}_{\mathrm{FF}}}+\overline{\mathrm{Id}_{d}})\circ(\mathrm{MHA}_{\theta_{\mathrm{MHA}}}+\overline{\mathrm{Id}_{d}}):(\mathbb{R}^{d})^{*}\to(\mathbb{R}^{d})^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Encoder Transformer)<span id="Thmdefinition7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With parameters <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=(\theta_{\mathrm{TE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>TE</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">𝐶𝐿𝑂𝑆𝐸</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=(\theta_{\mathrm{TE}}</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathrm{PE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>PE</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathrm{PE}}</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\theta^{(\ell)}_{\mathrm{MHA}})_{\ell=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>MHA</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\theta^{(\ell)}_{\mathrm{MHA}})_{\ell=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\theta^{(\ell)}_{\mathrm{FF}})_{\ell=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>FF</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\theta^{(\ell)}_{\mathrm{FF}})_{\ell=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>,<math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathrm{PROJ}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">𝑂𝑃𝐸𝑁</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>PROJ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathrm{PROJ}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the encoder transformer is:</span></p>
<table id="A6.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Enc}_{\theta}=\overline{\mathrm{PROJ}_{\theta_{\mathrm{PROJ}}}}\circ\left(\bigcirc_{\ell=1}^{L}\mathrm{EncTF}_{\theta^{(\ell)}_{\mathrm{MHA}},\theta^{(\ell)}_{\mathrm{FF}}}\right)\circ\big(\mathrm{TE}_{\theta_{\mathrm{TE}}}+\mathrm{PE}_{\theta_{\mathrm{PE}}}\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Enc</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>PROJ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>PROJ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">○</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>EncTF</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>MHA</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>FF</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>TE</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>TE</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>PE</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>PE</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Enc}_{\theta}=\overline{\mathrm{PROJ}_{\theta_{\mathrm{PROJ}}}}\circ\left(\bigcirc_{\ell=1}^{L}\mathrm{EncTF}_{\theta^{(\ell)}_{\mathrm{MHA}},\theta^{(\ell)}_{\mathrm{FF}}}\right)\circ\big(\mathrm{TE}_{\theta_{\mathrm{TE}}}+\mathrm{PE}_{\theta_{\mathrm{PE}}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The model applies embeddings, then <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> encoder layers, then position-wise projection to vocabulary logits. Output length equals input length <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Key Tool: Encoder Full-Access Sequence Processing (<span id="A7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span>)</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we develop Full-Access Sequence Processing for encoders (<span id="A7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span>), a programming language whose programs describe the construction process of seq-to-embedding functions that are equivalent to those computed by encoder-only Transformers. This extends the <span id="A7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FASP</span> framework originally developed for decoder-only Transformers in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2025)</a></cite>. Similar connections have also been established in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Weiss et al. (2021)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang &amp; Chiang (2024)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> is the key technical tool that will be used to prove <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (MDM Simulation of PRAM, Informal). ‣ 3.1 Power of Parallelism ‣ 3 A Theory of Masked Diffusion ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Left-to-Right v.s. Any-Order, Informal). ‣ 3.3 (Limited) Power of Any-Order Generation ‣ 3 A Theory of Masked Diffusion ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (AP-MDM Simulation of PRAM, Informal). ‣ 5.1 Universally Efficient Computation ‣ 5 The Power of Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Definition of <span id="A7.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span></h3>

<section id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notations.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that in <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Encoder Transformer Architecture ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>, we defined the position-indexed seq-to-embedding function space <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(B)</annotation></semantics></math> as the set of all functions <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> that map a sequence and a position index to an element in <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A7.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:(\Sigma^{*},[\cdot])\to B" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:(\Sigma^{*},[\cdot])\to B</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">That is, for every sequence <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})\in\Sigma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})\in\Sigma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and every index <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\mathbf{x},i)\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\mathbf{x},i)\in B</annotation></semantics></math>. We also define <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}=\cup_{d\in\mathbb{N}^{+}}\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em">∪</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=\cup_{d\in\mathbb{N}^{+}}\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> as the union of all such classes across real spaces of all output dimensions. For any position-indexed function <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in\mathcal{H}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in\mathcal{H}(B)</annotation></semantics></math>, its canonical extension <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\psi}:\Sigma^{*}\to B^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\psi}:\Sigma^{*}\to B^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\overline{\psi}(\mathbf{x})]_{i}=\psi(\mathbf{x},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\overline{\psi}(\mathbf{x})]_{i}=\psi(\mathbf{x},i)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[|\mathbf{x}|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[|\mathbf{x}|]</annotation></semantics></math>. This allows us to convert position-indexed functions to sequence-to-sequence functions when needed.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Also recall that <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PE}:\mathbb{N}^{+}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>PE</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PE}:\mathbb{N}^{+}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a positional embedding, and we additionally define <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>ACT</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a class of activation functions. We formally define <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 8</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Encoder-FASP)<span id="Thmdefinition8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">An <span id="Thmdefinition8.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program is a sequence of position-indexed seq-to-embedding functions <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{1},\ldots,\psi_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1},\ldots,\psi_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> constructed inductively. At each step <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>, the program maintains a set of defineable position-indexed seq-to-embedding functions <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and defines a new function by applying operators to functions in <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define the defineable functions at step <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{P}_{t}\triangleq\{\mathrm{TE},\mathrm{PE}\}\cup\{\psi_{i}\mid 1\leq i\leq t-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>TE</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>PE</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{P}_{t}\triangleq\{\mathrm{TE},\mathrm{PE}\}\cup\{\psi_{i}\mid 1\leq i\leq t-1\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TE}(\mathbf{x},i)=\mathrm{TE}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TE}(\mathbf{x},i)=\mathrm{TE}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PE}(\mathbf{x},i)=\mathrm{PE}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>PE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>PE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PE}(\mathbf{x},i)=\mathrm{PE}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> are the token and positional embedding functions respectively, viewed as position-indexed seq-to-embedding functions. <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at step <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> has to be defined by applying one of the following four <em id="Thmdefinition8.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">primitive</em> operators on already-defined functions from <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition8.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A7.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Concatenation</span><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">: For </span><math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi,\psi^{\prime}\in\mathcal{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi,\psi^{\prime}\in\mathcal{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d_{2}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, define</span></p>
<table id="A7.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\psi,\psi^{\prime}](\mathbf{x},i)=(\psi(\mathbf{x},i)\|\psi^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},i))\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}+d_{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\psi,\psi^{\prime}](\mathbf{x},i)=(\psi(\mathbf{x},i)\|\psi^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},i))\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}+d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> denotes vector concatenation.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Linear Projection</span><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">: For </span><math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in\mathcal{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in\mathcal{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and matrix </span><math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, define</span></p>
<table id="A7.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W\circ\psi)(\mathbf{x},i)=W\cdot\psi(\mathbf{x},i)\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W\circ\psi)(\mathbf{x},i)=W\cdot\psi(\mathbf{x},i)\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Nonlinear Activation</span><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span><span id="footnote6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup>
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">6</span>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                      We allow multi-variable activation functions like Gated ReLU (ReGLU), <math id="footnote6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\mapsto x[y]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\mapsto x[y]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For </span><math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in\mathcal{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in\mathcal{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>ACT</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, define</span></p>
<table id="A7.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma\circ\psi)(\mathbf{x},i)=\sigma(\psi(\mathbf{x},i))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma\circ\psi)(\mathbf{x},i)=\sigma(\psi(\mathbf{x},i))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Encoder Average-Hard Attention</span><span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">: For </span><math id="A7.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q,k\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q,k\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A7.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{d^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> where </span><math id="A7.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q,k,v\in\mathcal{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q,k,v\in\mathcal{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, define</span></p>
<table id="A7.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{aha}(q,k,v)(\mathbf{x},i)=\frac{1}{|A_{i}|}\sum_{j\in A_{i}}v(\mathbf{x},j)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">aha</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{aha}(q,k,v)(\mathbf{x},i)=\frac{1}{|A_{i}|}\sum_{j\in A_{i}}v(\mathbf{x},j)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.I1.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A7.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}=\arg\max_{j\in[|\mathbf{x}|]}\langle q(\mathbf{x},i),k(\mathbf{x},j)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}=\arg\max_{j\in[|\mathbf{x}|]}\langle q(\mathbf{x},i),k(\mathbf{x},j)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and ties are averaged uniformly. This attention can be seen as a pecial case of standard softmax attention with temperature approaching 0 </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Merrill et al., 2022</a><span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">)</span></cite><span id="A7.I1.i4.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Finally, when we want to use <span id="Thmdefinition8.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> to define a function mapping from a sequence of tokens <math id="Thmdefinition8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and a position index <math id="Thmdefinition8.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> to a single token in <math id="Thmdefinition8.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, we can define <math id="Thmdefinition8.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{|\Sigma|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{R}^{|\Sigma|})</annotation></semantics></math> and return <math id="Thmdefinition8.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max\psi(\mathbf{x},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max\psi(\mathbf{x},i)</annotation></semantics></math> (the token corresponding to the largest logit at the position <math id="Thmdefinition8.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>).<span id="footnote7" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">7</span></span>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  <span id="footnote7.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">We could assume an arbitrary order to break ties, but we omit this for simplicity. In our examples we always ensure the argmax is unique.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We denote the set of all position-indexed seq-to-embedding functions defineable by <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> with position embedding <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>PE</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PE}</annotation></semantics></math> and activation functions <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>ACT</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{E-FASP}[\mathrm{PE};\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E-FASP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>PE</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>ACT</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{E-FASP}[\mathrm{PE};\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>PE</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PE}</annotation></semantics></math> can be either <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">BiPE</span> or <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">SEQ</span>. The expressivity of <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> depends on the specific positional embedding and activation functions used.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Equivalence with Encoder Transformer</h3>

<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now establish the equivalence between <span id="A7.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> and encoder-only Transformers, and define the specific instantiation considered in the proof of this paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 9</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Encoder Transformer Function Class)<span id="Thmdefinition9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{\text{EncTF}[\mathrm{PE};\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">EncTF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>PE</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>ACT</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{\text{EncTF}[\mathrm{PE};\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}]}</annotation></semantics></math> be the class of seq-to-embedding functions that can be expressed by encoder-only Transformers of finite depth, where the positional embedding uses <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>PE</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PE}</annotation></semantics></math> (either <span id="Thmdefinition9.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">BiPE</span> or <span id="Thmdefinition9.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">SEQ</span>), feed-forward layers use activation functions from <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>ACT</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}</annotation></semantics></math>, attention layers use average-hard attention as defined in <a href="#A7.E39" title="In Item 4 ‣ Definition 8 (Encoder-FASP). ‣ Notations. ‣ G.1 Definition of E-FASP ‣ Appendix G Key Tool: Encoder Full-Access Sequence Processing (E-FASP) ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>, and all intermediate computations use finite precision arithmetic.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It is straightforward to see that both variants are equivalent to their corresponding Transformer function classes:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Equivalence of <span id="Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> and Encoder Transformers)<span id="Thmtheorem7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any positional embedding <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PE}\in\{\texttt{BiPE},\texttt{SEQ}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>PE</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">BiPE</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">SEQ</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PE}\in\{\texttt{BiPE},\texttt{SEQ}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and activation function class <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>ACT</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following equivalence holds:</span></p>
<table id="A7.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{E-FASP}[\mathrm{PE};\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}]=\mathcal{H}_{\text{EncTF}[\mathrm{PE};\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}]}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E-FASP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>PE</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>ACT</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">EncTF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>PE</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>ACT</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{E-FASP}[\mathrm{PE};\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}]=\mathcal{H}_{\text{EncTF}[\mathrm{PE};\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof Sketch.</h6>
<div id="A7.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forward direction<span id="A7.SS2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Each <span id="A7.SS2.p3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> primitive operator (concatenation, linear projection, nonlinear activation, encoder attention) directly corresponds to operations in encoder Transformers. Concatenation involves merging multiple smaller Transformers into a larger Transformer that produces the same output. </span>Reverse direction<span id="A7.SS2.p3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Any encoder Transformer can be expressed as an <span id="A7.SS2.p3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program by decomposing each layer into primitive operations.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The detailed proof, including the treatment of closed operators and inductive construction, is invariant to decoder or encoder Transformers, and thus is identical to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2025)</a></cite>; we omit the details.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, this equivalence holds because <span id="A7.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span>
programs capture the computational
structure of encoder Transformers. Each step in an
<span id="A7.SS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program corresponds to defining a new seq-to-
embedding function by applying primitive operators to
previously defined functions, which mirrors how
smaller Transformers are constructed into a deeper and wider Transformer that produces the same output. The Transformer corresponding to the program is of depth <math id="A7.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> (given constant <math id="A7.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>) and embedding size <math id="A7.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\max\{d_{\mathrm{PE}},d_{\mathrm{TE}}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>PE</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TE</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\max\{d_{\mathrm{PE}},d_{\mathrm{TE}}\})</annotation></semantics></math>, by construction in the proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 7 (Equivalence of E-FASP and Encoder Transformers). ‣ G.2 Equivalence with Encoder Transformer ‣ Appendix G Key Tool: Encoder Full-Access Sequence Processing (E-FASP) ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.3 </span>Two Variants of <span id="A7.SS3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span></h3>

<div id="A7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this paper, we consider two variants of <span id="A7.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> based on different positional embeddings, both using the same activation functions.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Variant 1: Binary Positional Encoding</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define <span id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> with binary positional embedding <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{BiPE}:\mathbb{N}^{+}\to\{0,1\}^{\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">BiPE</mtext><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{BiPE}:\mathbb{N}^{+}\to\{0,1\}^{\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A7.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{BiPE}(i)=\text{binary representation of }i\text{ using }\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil\text{ bits}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">BiPE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>binary representation of </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> using </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> bits</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{BiPE}(i)=\text{binary representation of }i\text{ using }\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil\text{ bits}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This representation uses <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> bits to represent all possible positions within the maximum context length <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(n)</annotation></semantics></math>, and aligns with the address representation in PRAM (<a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Parallel Random Access Machine ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>) for efficient bitwise arithmetic operations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Variant 2: Integer Positional Encoding</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also define <span id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> with integer positional embedding <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{SEQ}:\mathbb{N}^{+}\to\mathbb{N}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">SEQ</mtext><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{SEQ}:\mathbb{N}^{+}\to\mathbb{N}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A7.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{SEQ}(i)=i" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">SEQ</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{SEQ}(i)=i</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This is the identity mapping over <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{N}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{N}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> that directly uses the position index as a scalar feature, as considered in the original decoder-only <span id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FASP</span> framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Activation Functions</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both variants use the same class of activation functions <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}=\{\text{ReGLU}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>ACT</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>ReGLU</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathrm{ACT}}=\{\text{ReGLU}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where Gated ReLU (ReGLU) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dauphin et al., 2017</a>)</cite> is defined as <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ReGLU}(x,y)=x\cdot[y]_{+}=x\cdot\max(y,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>ReGLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ReGLU}(x,y)=x\cdot[y]_{+}=x\cdot\max(y,0)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. With Gated ReLU as the primitive activation, we can express ReLU and multiplication operations through the following identities:</p>
<table id="A7.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{ReLU}(x)=\text{ReGLU}(x,1),\quad x\times y=\text{ReGLU}(x,y)-\text{ReGLU}(x,-y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>ReLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>ReGLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>ReGLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>ReGLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{ReLU}(x)=\text{ReGLU}(x,1),\quad x\times y=\text{ReGLU}(x,y)-\text{ReGLU}(x,-y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, having ReGLU allows us to express both ReLU and multiplication (reverse is also true), making both variants equivalent:</p>
<table id="A7.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{BiPE};\text{ReGLU}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E-FASP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">BiPE</mtext><mo>;</mo><mtext>ReGLU</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{BiPE};\text{ReGLU}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E44.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{BiPE};[\cdot]_{+},\times]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E-FASP</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">BiPE</mtext><mo>;</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">×</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{BiPE};[\cdot]_{+},\times]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{SEQ};\text{ReGLU}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E-FASP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">SEQ</mtext><mo>;</mo><mtext>ReGLU</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{SEQ};\text{ReGLU}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E45.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{SEQ};[\cdot]_{+},\times]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E-FASP</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">SEQ</mtext><mo>;</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">×</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{SEQ};[\cdot]_{+},\times]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\cdot]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\cdot]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> are the ReLU and multiplication respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.4 </span>Original Supported Operators</h3>

<div id="A7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With the four primitive operators in <span id="A7.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> and the activation functions defined above, the following operators can be included in both variants <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{BiPE};[\cdot]_{+},\times]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E-FASP</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">BiPE</mtext><mo>;</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">×</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{BiPE};[\cdot]_{+},\times]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{SEQ};[\cdot]_{+},\times]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E-FASP</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">SEQ</mtext><mo>;</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">×</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{SEQ};[\cdot]_{+},\times]</annotation></semantics></math>, adapted from the decoder version of <span id="A7.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FASP</span>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Arithmetic Operators</em></p>
<ul id="A7.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A7.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{add}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\psi_{1}+\psi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">add</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{add}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\psi_{1}+\psi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>: Element-wise addition</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{minus}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\psi_{1}-\psi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">minus</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{minus}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\psi_{1}-\psi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>: Element-wise subtraction</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{multi}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\psi_{1}\times\psi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">multi</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{multi}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\psi_{1}\times\psi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>: Element-wise multiplication</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{max}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">max</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{max}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>: Element-wise maximum</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{min}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">min</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{min}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>: Element-wise minimum</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Boolean Operators</em>
For <math id="A7.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{1},\psi_{2}\in\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1},\psi_{2}\in\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A7.I3" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A7.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{and}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\min(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">and</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{and}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\min(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>: Logical AND</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{or}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\lnot(\lnot\psi_{1}\land\lnot\psi_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">or</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>¬</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{or}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\lnot(\lnot\psi_{1}\land\lnot\psi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>: Logical OR</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{not}(\psi)=1-\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">not</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{not}(\psi)=1-\psi</annotation></semantics></math>: Logical NOT</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{xor}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">xor</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{xor}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>: Logical XOR</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Comparison Operators</em>
For <math id="A7.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{1},\psi_{2}\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{Z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1},\psi_{2}\in\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{Z})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A7.I4" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A7.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{leq}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=[\psi_{2}-\psi_{1}+1]_{+}-[\psi_{2}-\psi_{1}]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">leq</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{leq}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=[\psi_{2}-\psi_{1}+1]_{+}-[\psi_{2}-\psi_{1}]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>: Less than or equal</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{geq}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\texttt{leq}(\psi_{2},\psi_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">geq</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">leq</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{geq}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\texttt{leq}(\psi_{2},\psi_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>: Greater than or equal</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{eq}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\texttt{leq}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})\land\texttt{leq}(\psi_{2},\psi_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">eq</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">leq</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">leq</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{eq}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\texttt{leq}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})\land\texttt{leq}(\psi_{2},\psi_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>: Equality</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{lt}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\texttt{leq}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">lt</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">leq</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{lt}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\texttt{leq}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2}-1)</annotation></semantics></math>: Less than</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I4.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{gt}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\texttt{lt}(\psi_{2},\psi_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">gt</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">lt</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{gt}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})=\texttt{lt}(\psi_{2},\psi_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>: Greater than</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Sequence Aggregation Operators</em></p>
<ul id="A7.I5" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A7.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{seq\_max}(\psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">seq_max</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{seq\_max}(\psi)</annotation></semantics></math>: Returns the maximum value across all positions in the sequence</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{seq\_min}(\psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">seq_min</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{seq\_min}(\psi)</annotation></semantics></math>: Returns the minimum value across all positions in the sequence</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{seq\_and}(\psi)=\texttt{seq\_min}(\psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">seq_and</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">seq_min</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{seq\_and}(\psi)=\texttt{seq\_min}(\psi)</annotation></semantics></math>: Logical AND across all positions</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I5.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{seq\_or}(\psi)=\texttt{seq\_max}(\psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">seq_or</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">seq_max</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{seq\_or}(\psi)=\texttt{seq\_max}(\psi)</annotation></semantics></math>: Logical OR across all positions</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I5.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I5.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I5.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I5.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{seq\_sum}(\psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">seq_sum</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{seq\_sum}(\psi)</annotation></semantics></math>: Sum of values across all positions (requires <math id="A7.I5.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log n</annotation></semantics></math> positional embedding)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I5.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I5.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I5.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I5.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\texttt{seq\_avg}(\psi)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\psi(x_{1:j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">seq_avg</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{seq\_avg}(\psi)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\psi(x_{1:j})</annotation></semantics></math>: Average across all positions</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Positional Operators</em></p>
<ul id="A7.I6" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A7.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\texttt{is\_first}(i)=\mathbf{1}[i=1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">is_first</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{is\_first}(i)=\mathbf{1}[i=1]</annotation></semantics></math>: Indicator for first position</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{inv\_seq\_len}(i)=1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">inv_seq_len</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{inv\_seq\_len}(i)=1/n</annotation></semantics></math>: Inverse of sequence length</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\texttt{is\_pos\_k}(i)=\mathbf{1}[i=k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">is_pos_k</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{is\_pos\_k}(i)=\mathbf{1}[i=k]</annotation></semantics></math>: Indicator for position <math id="A7.I6.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Control Flow Operators</em></p>
<ul id="A7.I7" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A7.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{if\_then\_else}(\psi_{\text{cond}},\psi_{\text{true}},\psi_{\text{false}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">if_then_else</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>true</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>false</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{if\_then\_else}(\psi_{\text{cond}},\psi_{\text{true}},\psi_{\text{false}})</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A7.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{ite}(\psi_{\text{cond}},\psi_{\text{true}},\psi_{\text{false}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ite</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>cond</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>true</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext>false</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{ite}(\psi_{\text{cond}},\psi_{\text{true}},\psi_{\text{false}})</annotation></semantics></math>: If-then-else conditional selection</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Attention Variants</em></p>
<ul id="A7.I8" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A7.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{aha}(q,k,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">aha</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{aha}(q,k,v)</annotation></semantics></math>: Standard average-hard attention (encoder bidirectional)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{rha}(q,k,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">rha</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{rha}(q,k,v)</annotation></semantics></math>: Rightmost-hard attention (breaks ties by selecting rightmost position)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I8.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{rightmost\_exact\_match}(q,k,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">rightmost_exact_match</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{rightmost\_exact\_match}(q,k,v)</annotation></semantics></math>: Rightmost exact match (returns default if no exact match)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.5 </span>Additional Operators and Justifications</h3>

<div id="A7.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next we give the semantics of some additional operators used in the PRAM simulation programs and justify their closure in the <span id="A7.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> framework.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS5.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Bitwise Arithmetic Operators</h4>

<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These operators are defined in the encoder-<span id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> framework using activations <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{[\cdot]_{+},\times\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">×</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{[\cdot]_{+},\times\}</annotation></semantics></math> (equivalently ReGLU) and are independent of the specific positional embedding choice. All inputs and outputs are position-indexed seq-to-embedding functions in <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\}^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\}^{m})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\mathbf{x},i)\in\{0,1\}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\mathbf{x},i)\in\{0,1\}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> encodes an <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-bit integer with LSB at coordinate 1. All arithmetic is modulo <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bitwise Addition.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{1},\psi_{2}\in\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\}^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1},\psi_{2}\in\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\}^{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, write at position <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x},i)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A7.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi_{1}(\mathbf{x},i)=:\mathbf{a}=(a_{1},\ldots,a_{m}),\quad\psi_{2}(\mathbf{x},i)=:\mathbf{b}=(b_{1},\ldots,b_{m})\in\{0,1\}^{m}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1}(\mathbf{x},i)=:\mathbf{a}=(a_{1},\ldots,a_{m}),\quad\psi_{2}(\mathbf{x},i)=:\mathbf{b}=(b_{1},\ldots,b_{m})\in\{0,1\}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Bitwise addition is defined as adding two <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-bit integers modulo <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. This can be constructed using the primitive operators (and other operators that are already defined) in <a href="#Thmdefinition8" title="Definition 8 (Encoder-FASP). ‣ Notations. ‣ G.1 Definition of E-FASP ‣ Appendix G Key Tool: Encoder Full-Access Sequence Processing (E-FASP) ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, which follows an approach similar to standard carry-lookahead, and is a constant-depth, polylogarithmic-width construction:</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Define for <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math> the local propagate/generate bits:</p>
<table id="A7.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}=a_{k}\oplus b_{k}=a_{k}+b_{k}-2a_{k}b_{k},\quad g_{k}=a_{k}\wedge b_{k}=a_{k}b_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}=a_{k}\oplus b_{k}=a_{k}+b_{k}-2a_{k}b_{k},\quad g_{k}=a_{k}\wedge b_{k}=a_{k}b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{j}=\sum_{t\leq j}p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{j}=\sum_{t\leq j}p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math> (computed by a single linear layer). For <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j&lt;i\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j&lt;i\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>, define the interval-all-ones gate:</p>
<table id="A7.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{j,i}=\mathrm{eq}_{0}\left((S_{i-1}-S_{j})-((i-1)-j)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>eq</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{j,i}=\mathrm{eq}_{0}\left((S_{i-1}-S_{j})-((i-1)-j)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{eq}_{k}(u):=2\left([u-(k-\frac{1}{2})]_{+}-2[u-k]_{+}+[u-(k+\frac{1}{2})]_{+}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>eq</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{eq}_{k}(u):=2\left([u-(k-\frac{1}{2})]_{+}-2[u-k]_{+}+[u-(k+\frac{1}{2})]_{+}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> equals 1 at <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=k</annotation></semantics></math> and 0 at all other integers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The carry into bit <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A7.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}=\begin{cases}0,&amp;i=1\\
1-\mathrm{eq}_{0}\left(\sum_{j=1}^{i-1}g_{j}Q_{j,i}\right),&amp;i\geq 2\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>eq</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}=\begin{cases}0,&amp;i=1\\
1-\mathrm{eq}_{0}\left(\sum_{j=1}^{i-1}g_{j}Q_{j,i}\right),&amp;i\geq 2\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The sum bits are <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}=p_{i}\oplus C_{i}=p_{i}+C_{i}-2p_{i}C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}=p_{i}\oplus C_{i}=p_{i}+C_{i}-2p_{i}C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define:</p>
<table id="A7.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{bit\_add}_{m}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})(\mathbf{x},i):=\mathbf{s}=(s_{1},\ldots,s_{m})\in\{0,1\}^{m}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">bit_add</mtext><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{bit\_add}_{m}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2})(\mathbf{x},i):=\mathbf{s}=(s_{1},\ldots,s_{m})\in\{0,1\}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bitwise Subtraction.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{1},\psi_{2}\in\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\}^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1},\psi_{2}\in\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\}^{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, define:</p>
<table id="A7.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{bit\_minus}_{m}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2}):=\texttt{bit\_add}_{m}(\psi_{1},\neg\psi_{2})\dotplus 1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">bit_minus</mtext><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">bit_add</mtext><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∔</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{bit\_minus}_{m}(\psi_{1},\psi_{2}):=\texttt{bit\_add}_{m}(\psi_{1},\neg\psi_{2})\dotplus 1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\neg" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>¬</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\neg</annotation></semantics></math> is bitwise NOT (elementwise <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1-\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\cdot</annotation></semantics></math>) and “<math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dotplus 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∔</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dotplus 1</annotation></semantics></math>” adds the constant vector <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{1}=(1,0,\ldots,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{1}=(1,0,\ldots,0)</annotation></semantics></math> via the same <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{bit\_add}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">bit_add</mtext><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{bit\_add}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Logical Shifts.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\}^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\}^{m})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\}^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\}^{m})</annotation></semantics></math>. At position <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x},i)</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}=\psi(\mathbf{x},i)=(a_{1},\ldots,a_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}=\psi(\mathbf{x},i)=(a_{1},\ldots,a_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> and define the shift amount:</p>
<table id="A7.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\mathrm{int}(\tau)=\sum_{r=1}^{m}2^{r-1}\tau_{r}\in\{0,\ldots,m\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\mathrm{int}(\tau)=\sum_{r=1}^{m}2^{r-1}\tau_{r}\in\{0,\ldots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>, we define:</p>
<table id="A7.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[\texttt{shift\_left}_{m}(\psi,\tau)]_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">shift_left</mtext><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[\texttt{shift\_left}_{m}(\psi,\tau)]_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{s=0}^{\min\{m,k-1\}}\mathrm{eq}_{s}(t)\cdot a_{k-s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>eq</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{s=0}^{\min\{m,k-1\}}\mathrm{eq}_{s}(t)\cdot a_{k-s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[\texttt{shift\_right}_{m}(\psi,\tau)]_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">shift_right</mtext><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[\texttt{shift\_right}_{m}(\psi,\tau)]_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{s=0}^{\min\{m,m-k\}}\mathrm{eq}_{s}(t)\cdot a_{k+s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>eq</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{s=0}^{\min\{m,m-k\}}\mathrm{eq}_{s}(t)\cdot a_{k+s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where out-of-range indices are treated as 0, and <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{eq}_{s}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>eq</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{eq}_{s}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the integer-equality gate realized by three ReLUs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Complexity Analysis.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All operators act locally at each position on <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\}^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\{0,1\}^{m})</annotation></semantics></math> without cross-position communication, and are composed from <span id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> primitives. Throughout <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\Theta(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\Theta(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The witness enumeration method for bitwise addition requires: <span id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(i)</span> one linear layer for <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p,g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p,g)</annotation></semantics></math> and prefix sums <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(ii)</span> one nonlinear layer for witnesses <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{j,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{j,i}</annotation></semantics></math> (each uses 3 ReLUs) and products <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{j}Q_{j,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{j}Q_{j,i}</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(iii)</span> linear aggregation and threshold for carries <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(iv)</span> local polynomial for <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}=p_{i}\oplus C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}=p_{i}\oplus C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. This achieves constant depth (3-4 layers) and width <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2})=\mathcal{O}((\log n)^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2})=\mathcal{O}((\log n)^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> (polylogarithmic in <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>). Bitwise subtraction uses two’s complement and reuses the same addition circuit with identical complexity bounds. Logical shifts compute the shift amount <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and all candidate shifts in parallel, then use equality gates for selection, also achieving constant depth and <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> width.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">All constructions use only <span id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> primitives (linear projections, ReLU/ReGLU activations, multiplication). By the equivalence established in <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Key Tool: Encoder Full-Access Sequence Processing (E-FASP) ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>, these are realizable by constant-depth encoder Transformers.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Instruction Access Operations.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This operator enables instruction fetching from memory by address lookup, which is essential for PRAM simulation.</p>
<table id="A7.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{get\_instruction}(\mathbf{x},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>get</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>instruction</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{get\_instruction}(\mathbf{x},i)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathrm{bin}(W_{\mathrm{INSTR}}\circ\mathrm{ite}(\mathrm{is\_addr}(\mathbf{x},\cdot),\mathrm{bin}(\mathrm{TE}(\mathbf{x},\cdot)),\mathbf{0}_{w}))(\mathbf{x},i)\in\{0,1\}^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>bin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>INSTR</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>ite</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>is</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>addr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>bin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathrm{bin}(W_{\mathrm{INSTR}}\circ\mathrm{ite}(\mathrm{is\_addr}(\mathbf{x},\cdot),\mathrm{bin}(\mathrm{TE}(\mathbf{x},\cdot)),\mathbf{0}_{w}))(\mathbf{x},i)\in\{0,1\}^{w}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mathrm{INSTR}}:\mathbb{R}^{w}\to\mathbb{R}^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>INSTR</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mathrm{INSTR}}:\mathbb{R}^{w}\to\mathbb{R}^{w}</annotation></semantics></math> is a learned linear transformation (MLP layer) that maps address bits to instruction bits. This operator first extracts the address bits from address positions (even positions ¿ 1) by converting their token embeddings to binary representations, then applies the instruction lookup transformation <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mathrm{INSTR}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>INSTR</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mathrm{INSTR}}</annotation></semantics></math> to produce the corresponding instruction encoding. The PRAM instruction set (LOAD, STORE, ADD, SUB, etc., as defined in <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Parallel Random Access Machine ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>) is hardcoded into the parameters of <math id="A7.SS5.SSSx1.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mathrm{INSTR}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>INSTR</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mathrm{INSTR}}</annotation></semantics></math> during training, enabling the model to perform instruction fetching through learned address-to-instruction mappings.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (MDM Simulation of PRAM, Informal). ‣ 3.1 Power of Parallelism ‣ 3 A Theory of Masked Diffusion ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 8</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(MDM Simulation of PRAM, Formal)<span id="Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any PRAM program <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=(I_{0},\dots,I_{\ell},\mathrm{addr})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>addr</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=(I_{0},\dots,I_{\ell},\mathrm{addr})</annotation></semantics></math> (with finite number of instructions <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, and is uniform for all processors and input size <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>), that on input <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\text{val}}\in\mathbb{U}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">val</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\text{val}}\in\mathbb{U}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with corresponding address <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\text{addr}}\in\mathcal{A}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">addr</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\text{addr}}\in\mathcal{A}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> that runs in <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(n)</annotation></semantics></math> parallel time using at most <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)</annotation></semantics></math> processors and outputs <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{PRAM}_{\mathcal{P}}(\mathbf{x}_{\text{addr}},\mathbf{x}_{\text{val}})\in\mathbb{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">PRAM</mtext><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">addr</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">val</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕌</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{PRAM}_{\mathcal{P}}(\mathbf{x}_{\text{addr}},\mathbf{x}_{\text{val}})\in\mathbb{U}</annotation></semantics></math> per procedure described in <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Parallel Random Access Machine ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>, there exists a bijection <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathbb{U}\cup\mathcal{A}\rightarrow\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕌</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathbb{U}\cup\mathcal{A}\rightarrow\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and a special token <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{[SEP]}\in\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[SEP]</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{[SEP]}\in\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, and a MDM with constant depth and <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(n)</annotation></semantics></math> embedding size encoder-only Transformer, on input <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}=((\mathbf{z}_{2i},\mathbf{z}_{2i+1})_{i=0}^{n-1},\texttt{[SEP]})\in\Sigma^{2n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[SEP]</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=((\mathbf{z}_{2i},\mathbf{z}_{2i+1})_{i=0}^{n-1},\texttt{[SEP]})\in\Sigma^{2n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{2i}=\phi(\mathbf{x}_{\text{addr},i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">addr</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{2i}=\phi(\mathbf{x}_{\text{addr},i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{2i+1}=\phi(\mathbf{x}_{\text{val},i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">val</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{2i+1}=\phi(\mathbf{x}_{\text{val},i})</annotation></semantics></math>, padded to <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(P(n)\times T(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(P(n)\times T(n))</annotation></semantics></math> context length, outputs <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\text{PRAM}_{\mathcal{P}}(\mathbf{x}_{\text{addr}},\mathbf{x}_{\text{val}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">PRAM</mtext><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">addr</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">val</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\text{PRAM}_{\mathcal{P}}(\mathbf{x}_{\text{addr}},\mathbf{x}_{\text{val}}))</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T(n))</annotation></semantics></math> decoding steps.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof demonstrates that AO-MDM can simulate any PRAM algorithm. The construction is based on <span id="A8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span>, the programming language we developed, whose definable programs are equivalent to encoder-only Transformer function class (see <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Key Tool: Encoder Full-Access Sequence Processing (E-FASP) ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>). We prove <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (MDM Simulation of PRAM, Informal). ‣ 3.1 Power of Parallelism ‣ 3 A Theory of Masked Diffusion ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> by: <span id="A8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1)</span> defining the setup and input format for PRAM simulation; <span id="A8.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2)</span> constructing an <span id="A8.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program that simulates PRAM execution in <a href="#alg2" title="In Termination and Complexity. ‣ E.1 Definition and Execution Process of Word-RAM ‣ Appendix E Parallel Random Access Machine ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Choice of Architecture / <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> Variant</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For this simulation, we use the <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{SEQ};[\cdot]_{+},\times]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E-FASP</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">SEQ</mtext><mo>;</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">×</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{SEQ};[\cdot]_{+},\times]</annotation></semantics></math> variant with integer positional encoding rather than the binary variant. This choice is crucial because MDM’s context length can be exponentially large (e.g., for NP-hard problems), while PRAM’s actual memory usage remains polynomial. Using <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log n</annotation></semantics></math> bits to represent positions would be insufficient when the context length <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> itself grows exponentially with the problem size, even though PRAM addresses can still be represented in <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log S(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log S(n)</annotation></semantics></math> bits. To avoid confusion between MDM’s context length and PRAM’s memory space, we use <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\text{MDM}}(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>MDM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\text{MDM}}(n)</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the maximum context length and reserve <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(n)</annotation></semantics></math> for PRAM’s memory space.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Input Format</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The input that encodes the PRAM’s initial memory state is a sequence <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{2n+2})\in\Sigma^{2n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{2n+2})\in\Sigma^{2n+2}</annotation></semantics></math> of discrete tokens from the vocabulary <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=\Theta(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\Theta(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math> be the word width and recall from <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Parallel Random Access Machine ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> that the address width <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil\leq w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\lceil\log_{2}S(n)\rceil\leq w</annotation></semantics></math> (addresses fit within words). The sequence has length <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n+2=1+2n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n+2=1+2n+1</annotation></semantics></math> where:</p>
<table id="A8.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E56.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\in\Sigma\quad\text{(processor count token)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>(processor count token)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\Sigma\quad\text{(processor count token)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{2i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{2i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E57.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\in\Sigma\quad\text{(address token)}\quad\text{for }i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>(address token)</mtext><mtext>for </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\Sigma\quad\text{(address token)}\quad\text{for }i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{2i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{2i+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E58.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\in\Sigma\quad\text{(data token)}\quad\text{for }i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>(data token)</mtext><mtext>for </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\Sigma\quad\text{(data token)}\quad\text{for }i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{2n+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{2n+2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E59.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\texttt{[SEP]}\quad\text{(separator token)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[SEP]</mtext><mtext>(separator token)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\texttt{[SEP]}\quad\text{(separator token)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Through token embedding <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TE}:\Sigma\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TE}:\Sigma\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and subsequent linear projections, these discrete tokens are mapped to their semantic bit representations:</p>
<table id="A8.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{TE}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{TE}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mapsto P(n)\in\{0,1\}^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mapsto P(n)\in\{0,1\}^{w}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{TE}(x_{2i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{TE}(x_{2i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E61.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mapsto\text{addr}_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{w}\quad\text{(address bits)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mtext>addr</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup><mtext>(address bits)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mapsto\text{addr}_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{w}\quad\text{(address bits)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{TE}(x_{2i+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{TE}(x_{2i+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E62.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mapsto\text{val}_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{w}\quad\text{(data bits)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mtext>val</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup><mtext>(data bits)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mapsto\text{val}_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{w}\quad\text{(data bits)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">for <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>. The <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[SEP]</span> token serves as a separator with special meaning in the computation trace, as detailed in the next subsection. Following the standard MDM notation from <a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminary ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the actual input to the MDM is the padded sequence <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}=(x_{0,1},x_{0,2},\ldots,x_{0,S_{\text{MDM}}(n)})\in\bar{\Sigma}^{S_{\text{MDM}}(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>MDM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>MDM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}=(x_{0,1},x_{0,2},\ldots,x_{0,S_{\text{MDM}}(n)})\in\bar{\Sigma}^{S_{\text{MDM}}(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Sigma}=\Sigma\cup\{\textsf{M}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Sigma}=\Sigma\cup\{\textsf{M}\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A8.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{0,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{0,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E63.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{j}\quad\text{for }j=1,\ldots,2n+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mtext>for </mtext><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{j}\quad\text{for }j=1,\ldots,2n+2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{0,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{0,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E64.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\textsf{M}\quad\text{for }j=2n+3,\ldots,S_{\text{MDM}}(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mtext>for </mtext><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>MDM</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\textsf{M}\quad\text{for }j=2n+3,\ldots,S_{\text{MDM}}(n)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We aim to show that there exists an encoder-only Transformer that, given the initial memory state of a PRAM as input, can output the exact same result as the PRAM algorithm after <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{MDM}}(n)=\mathcal{O}(T(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>MDM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{MDM}}(n)=\mathcal{O}(T(n))</annotation></semantics></math> decoding steps. The Transformer will have constant depth and context length <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(S_{\text{MDM}}(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>MDM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(S_{\text{MDM}}(n))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\text{MDM}}(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>MDM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\text{MDM}}(n)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the MDM’s context budget.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We next provide an overview of the construction:</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Processor State and Computation Log Representation:</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we state the representation of processor state and computation log as tokens. We represent each processor’s state and one round of computation using a fixed number of tokens: program counter (1 token), register file (5 tokens), and computation log (2 tokens), for a total of 8 tokens per processor.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Program Counter (PC):</em> A single word encoding the current instruction address.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Register File:</em> We maintain exactly 5 registers, each storing one word. This provides sufficient computational capacity while keeping the representation tractable.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Computation Log:</em> This log is populated only when executing <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">STORE [s],r</span> instructions, recording the target address and stored value. For all other instructions, the log remains empty (represented by special tokens).</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The computation trace for one parallel round can be represented as:</p>
<table id="A8.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\texttt{[SEP]}\;\langle\texttt{PC}_{1},\texttt{R}_{1,1},\ldots,\texttt{R}_{1,5},\texttt{Addr}_{1},\texttt{Val}_{1}\rangle\;\langle\texttt{PC}_{2},\texttt{R}_{2,1},\ldots,\texttt{R}_{2,5},\texttt{Addr}_{2},\texttt{Val}_{2}\rangle\;\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[SEP]</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">PC</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Addr</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Val</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">PC</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Addr</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Val</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\texttt{[SEP]}\;\langle\texttt{PC}_{1},\texttt{R}_{1,1},\ldots,\texttt{R}_{1,5},\texttt{Addr}_{1},\texttt{Val}_{1}\rangle\;\langle\texttt{PC}_{2},\texttt{R}_{2,1},\ldots,\texttt{R}_{2,5},\texttt{Addr}_{2},\texttt{Val}_{2}\rangle\;\ldots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[SEP]</span> serves as a separator token to distinguish different computation rounds and there are a total of <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)</annotation></semantics></math> independent processors. Each processor <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\ldots,P(n)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\ldots,P(n)\}</annotation></semantics></math> contributes an 8-tuple <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\texttt{PC}_{i},\texttt{R}_{i,1},\texttt{R}_{i,2},\texttt{R}_{i,3},\texttt{R}_{i,4},\texttt{R}_{i,5},\texttt{Addr}_{i},\texttt{Val}_{i}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">PC</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Addr</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Val</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\texttt{PC}_{i},\texttt{R}_{i,1},\texttt{R}_{i,2},\texttt{R}_{i,3},\texttt{R}_{i,4},\texttt{R}_{i,5},\texttt{Addr}_{i},\texttt{Val}_{i}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> representing its program counter, five register values, and memory write operation (address and value). The trace thus contains exactly <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)</annotation></semantics></math> such 8-tuples per parallel round.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Processor Assignment and Role Identification.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm begins by determining whether the current position contains a mask token (i.e. <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{is\_mask}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>is</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>mask</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{is\_mask}</annotation></semantics></math>). If the position is a mask token (<span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Branch 1</span>), the algorithm continues by computing the distance to the nearest preceding <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[SEP]</span> token. If the position is not a mask token (<span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Branch 2</span>), it indicates this position has already been unmasked (computation has already finished), and the algorithm returns the input token (or a all zero vector) which will not be unmasked per definition of MDM <a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminary ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To identify the processor ID, we find the rightmost <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[SEP]</span> token to the left of the current position (i.e. <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rightmost\_sep\_pos}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rightmost</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sep</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>pos</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rightmost\_sep\_pos}</annotation></semantics></math>) and compute the distance between them (i.e. <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{distance\_to\_sep}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>distance</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>to</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sep</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{distance\_to\_sep}</annotation></semantics></math>). If this distance <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;8\times P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;8\times P(n)</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Branch 1.1</span>), the position does not participate in the current computation round as it is not a token that should be “unmasked” in this round, in this case, the algorithm returns a special embedding (a all zero vector), which results in uniform distribution during prediction and smallest confidence, ensuring that the MDM will not select this position for unmasking; if the distance <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=8\times P(n)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=8\times P(n)+1</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Branch 1.2</span>), this position return the embedding of <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[SEP]</span>, preparing for the next computation round; otherwise if the distance <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;8\times P(n)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;8\times P(n)+1</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Branch 1.3</span>), the position participates in the computation of the current round.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For those positions participating in the current computation round. The corresponding processor ID (i.e. <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{processor\_id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>processor</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>id</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{processor\_id}</annotation></semantics></math>) is obtained by right-shifting <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{distance\_to\_sep}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>distance</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>to</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sep</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{distance\_to\_sep}</annotation></semantics></math> by 3 bits with zero-padding on the left (since each processor corresponds to exactly 8 tokens). The rightmost 3 bits represent the position within that processor (i.e. <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{inner\_processor\_id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>inner</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>processor</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>id</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{inner\_processor\_id}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Initialization of Processor State.</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We need to initialize the initial state of all processors at the beginning. This is determined by the current number of <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[SEP]</span> tokens in the sequence. Specifically, when the current position is a mask token and there is exactly one <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[SEP]</span> token (i.e. <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{seq\_sum}(\mathrm{is\_sep})==1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>seq</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sum</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>is</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sep</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{seq\_sum}(\mathrm{is\_sep})==1</annotation></semantics></math>) (<span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Branch 3</span>), we consider this the initialization state. All program counters are set to 0, all registers are set to 0, and all memory locations are set to 0.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Fetch Instruction and Execution (Main Loop).</h5>

<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">According to the processor ID and inner processor position, the algorithm fetches the instruction from the instruction memory (i.e. <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{get\_instruction}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>get</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>instruction</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{get\_instruction}</annotation></semantics></math>), which is hard-coded into the parameters of the model, and execute it (using <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{execute}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>execute</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{execute}</annotation></semantics></math>). Different instructions yields different execution semantics, and sequently different <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> token state. Finally, according to the <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{inner\_processor\_id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>inner</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>processor</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>id</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{inner\_processor\_id}</annotation></semantics></math>, the algorithm chooses what to return. The algorithm terminates when the PC of all processors are HALT.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now formally construct an <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program that simulates PRAM execution (the single-processor algorithm detailed in <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Parallel Random Access Machine ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>). The semantics meanings and justifications of operators used in the program are summarized in <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Key Tool: Encoder Full-Access Sequence Processing (E-FASP) ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>. The only two global operators are <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">seq_sum</span> and <span id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">rightmost_exact_match</span> implementable by attention , otherwise are all local operators implementable by polylog-width constant-depth MLPs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The context length of MDM used by this construction is <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\text{MDM}}(n)=\mathcal{O}(T_{\text{par}}(n)\times P(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>MDM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>par</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\text{MDM}}(n)=\mathcal{O}(T_{\text{par}}(n)\times P(n))</annotation></semantics></math>, the decoding steps is <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{MDM}}(n)=\mathcal{O}(T_{\text{par}}(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>MDM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>par</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{MDM}}(n)=\mathcal{O}(T_{\text{par}}(n))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{par}}(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>par</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{par}}(n)</annotation></semantics></math> is the parallel time complexity and <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)</annotation></semantics></math> is the processor count. For the constructed Transformer, embedding size is <math id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(n)</annotation></semantics></math> and depth is a constant.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<div id="A8.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p4.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_python ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_comment ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">#<span id="lstnumberx1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>----------------------<span id="lstnumberx1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>Initialization<span id="lstnumberx1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>----------------------</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">is_sep</span><span id="lstnumberx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">   </span><span id="lstnumberx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">TE</span><span id="lstnumberx2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">==</span><span id="lstnumberx2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">embed</span><span id="lstnumberx2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">([</span><span id="lstnumberx2.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">SEP</span><span id="lstnumberx2.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">]))</span>
</div>
