<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 (Un)Scalability to Hard Tasks ‣ 3 A Theory of Masked Diffusion ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The result stems from MDM’s total amount of computation being bounded by <math id="A9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(n)</annotation></semantics></math> in both total steps (<math id="A9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(n)\leq S(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(n)\leq S(n)</annotation></semantics></math>) and per-step capacity (polynomial embedding size), preventing it from solving problems requiring greater computational resources.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fix an encoder-only MDM with context length <math id="A9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(n)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(n)</annotation></semantics></math> decoding steps. Throughout we assume constant depth/heads and log-precision arithmetic with hidden width <math id="A9.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=\Theta(\log(S(n)+T(n)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=\Theta(\log(S(n)+T(n)))</annotation></semantics></math> (binary positional code), as in our setup. Particularly, at each decoding step the model re-encodes a length-<math id="A9.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(n)</annotation></semantics></math> sequence. A single forward pass is dominated by self-attention: for each position <math id="A9.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> we form a query in <math id="A9.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and take dot products with all <math id="A9.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(n)</annotation></semantics></math> keys, then take the value-weighted sum. Counting FLOPs, one attention head costs</p>
<table id="A9.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Theta\big(S(n)\cdot S(n)\cdot d\big)=\Theta\!\big(S(n)^{2}\log(S(n)+T(n))\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Theta\big(S(n)\cdot S(n)\cdot d\big)=\Theta\!\big(S(n)^{2}\log(S(n)+T(n))\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and the multi-head/multi-layer constants only change the leading constant. The position-wise MLP adds <math id="A9.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(S(n)\cdot\operatorname{poly}(d))=\Theta\!\big(S(n)\operatorname{polylog}(S(n)+T(n))\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>poly</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>polylog</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(S(n)\cdot\operatorname{poly}(d))=\Theta\!\big(S(n)\operatorname{polylog}(S(n)+T(n))\big)</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs and is lower order when <math id="A9.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(n)\gg d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(n)\gg d</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus one decoding step costs</p>
<table id="A9.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A9.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A9.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}\big(S(n)^{2}\big)\quad\text{FLOPs,}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>FLOPs,</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}\big(S(n)^{2}\big)\quad\text{FLOPs,}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A9.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> suppresses polylog factors in <math id="A9.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(n)+T(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(n)+T(n)</annotation></semantics></math>. Over <math id="A9.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(n)</annotation></semantics></math> steps the total compute is <math id="A9.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}\!\big(S(n)^{2}\,T(n)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}\!\big(S(n)^{2}\,T(n)\big)</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, when each step reveals at least one token (or a constant number), we have <math id="A9.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(n)\leq S(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(n)\leq S(n)</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding the unified cubic bound <math id="A9.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(S(n)^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{O}}(S(n)^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence any problem that needs <math id="A9.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\!\big(S(n)^{3}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.488em;" width="0.488em"><mi>ω</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\!\big(S(n)^{3}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> serial time cannot be solved by MDM in the <math id="A9.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S(n),T(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S(n),T(n))</annotation></semantics></math> regime stated.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix J </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Left-to-Right v.s. Any-Order, Informal). ‣ 3.3 (Limited) Power of Any-Order Generation ‣ 3 A Theory of Masked Diffusion ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall <a href="#Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 3 (Masked-ARM). ‣ 3.3 (Limited) Power of Any-Order Generation ‣ 3 A Theory of Masked Diffusion ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we defined <span id="A10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Masked-ARM</span> as an autoregressive model with encoder-only Transformer architecture that pads the input sequence with mask tokens to the maximum context length, which is also equivalent to a MDM with a fixed order (left-to-right) generation and generating one token at a time. Consider an AO-MDM with input format <math id="A10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> followed by a special separator token <span id="A10.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[SEP]</span> at position <math id="A10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AO-MDM Intermediate State:</span> At any intermediate generation step, the AO-MDM state can be represented as <math id="A10.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}=(z_{1},\ldots,z_{S(n)})\in\bar{\Sigma}^{S(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}=(z_{1},\ldots,z_{S(n)})\in\bar{\Sigma}^{S(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A10.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Sigma}=\Sigma\cup\{\textsf{M}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Sigma}=\Sigma\cup\{\textsf{M}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The sequence structure is:</p>
<table id="A10.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E68.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{j}\quad\text{for }j\in[n]\quad\text{(fixed input portion)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mtext>for </mtext><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mtext>(fixed input portion)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{j}\quad\text{for }j\in[n]\quad\text{(fixed input portion)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E69.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\texttt{[SEP]}\quad\text{(separator)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[SEP]</mtext><mtext>(separator)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\texttt{[SEP]}\quad\text{(separator)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E70.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\in\Sigma\cup\{\textsf{M}\}\quad\text{for }j\in\{n+2,\ldots,S(n)\}\quad\text{(generation region)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mtext>(generation region)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\Sigma\cup\{\textsf{M}\}\quad\text{for }j\in\{n+2,\ldots,S(n)\}\quad\text{(generation region)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A10.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A10.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=(d_{1},d_{2},\ldots,d_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=(d_{1},d_{2},\ldots,d_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the sequence of positions that have been decoded (unmasked) by the AO-MDM in chronological order, where <math id="A10.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}\in\{n+2,\ldots,S(n)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}\in\{n+2,\ldots,S(n)\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{d_{i}}\neq\textsf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{d_{i}}\neq\textsf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A10.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[k]</annotation></semantics></math>. The ordering reflects the temporal sequence in which the AO-MDM performed the unmasking operations.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 10</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Position/Content Tokens and Address Encoding)<span id="Thmdefinition10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> be the base vocabulary. We reserve a subset <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}\subseteq\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>pos</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}\subseteq\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> for position tokens and define a bijection <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{encode}:\{1,\ldots,S(n)\}\to\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>encode</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>pos</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{encode}:\{1,\ldots,S(n)\}\to\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}</annotation></semantics></math> with inverse <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dec\_pos}:\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}\to\{1,\ldots,S(n)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>pos</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>pos</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dec\_pos}:\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}\to\{1,\ldots,S(n)\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each decoded position <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A10.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{addr}_{d_{i}}:=\mathrm{encode}(d_{i})\in\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}\subseteq\Sigma,\qquad\texttt{tok}_{d_{i}}:=z_{d_{i}}\in\Sigma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">addr</mtext><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>encode</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>pos</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tok</mtext><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{addr}_{d_{i}}:=\mathrm{encode}(d_{i})\in\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}\subseteq\Sigma,\qquad\texttt{tok}_{d_{i}}:=z_{d_{i}}\in\Sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus both address tokens and content tokens are drawn from the original vocabulary <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. We also reserve a subset <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\mathrm{op}}\subseteq\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\mathrm{op}}\subseteq\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> for operator tokens used later for AP-MDM edits (<a href="#S4" title="4 Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Masked-ARM Simulation:</span> For each decoded token at position <math id="A10.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Masked-ARM represents it using a 2-tuple:</p>
<table id="A10.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\texttt{addr}_{d_{i}},\texttt{tok}_{d_{i}}\rangle=\langle\text{encode}(d_{i}),z_{d_{i}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">addr</mtext><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tok</mtext><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>encode</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\texttt{addr}_{d_{i}},\texttt{tok}_{d_{i}}\rangle=\langle\text{encode}(d_{i}),z_{d_{i}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A10.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{encode}(d_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>encode</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{encode}(d_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is a token representation of the positional index <math id="A10.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A10.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the actual decoded token. The target Masked-ARM sequence to be constructed is:</p>
<table id="A10.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{y}_{\text{ARM}}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n},\texttt{[SEP]},\texttt{addr}_{d_{1}},\texttt{tok}_{d_{1}},\ldots,\texttt{addr}_{d_{k}},\texttt{tok}_{d_{k}},\underbrace{\textsf{M},\ldots,\textsf{M}}_{\text{remaining positions}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mtext>ARM</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[SEP]</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">addr</mtext><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tok</mtext><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">addr</mtext><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tok</mtext><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>remaining positions</mtext></munder><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{y}_{\text{ARM}}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n},\texttt{[SEP]},\texttt{addr}_{d_{1}},\texttt{tok}_{d_{1}},\ldots,\texttt{addr}_{d_{k}},\texttt{tok}_{d_{k}},\underbrace{\textsf{M},\ldots,\textsf{M}}_{\text{remaining positions}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where the sequence <math id="A10.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=(d_{1},d_{2},\ldots,d_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=(d_{1},d_{2},\ldots,d_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the chronological order of AO-MDM’s decoding operations. The Masked-ARM sequence has total length <math id="A10.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2S(n)-n-1=\mathcal{O}(S(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2S(n)-n-1=\mathcal{O}(S(n))</annotation></semantics></math>, since each AO-MDM token requires two tokens (address and content) in the Masked-ARM representation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Induction:</span> To prove We prove by induction that for any AO-MDM, there exists a corresponding Masked-ARM that can simulate the AO-MDM’s generation process step by step for arbitrary input sequences.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 9</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(AO-MDM Simulation by Masked-ARM)<span id="Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any AO-MDM, there exists a corresponding Masked-ARM such that: for any input sequence <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> and any intermediate state of the AO-MDM with decoded sequence <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=(d_{1},d_{2},\ldots,d_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=(d_{1},d_{2},\ldots,d_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, the Masked-ARM, starting from the corresponding intermediate state <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{\text{ARM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ARM</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{\text{ARM}}</annotation></semantics></math>, can generate the next address-token pair <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\texttt{addr}_{d_{k+1}},\texttt{tok}_{d_{k+1}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">addr</mtext><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tok</mtext><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\texttt{addr}_{d_{k+1}},\texttt{tok}_{d_{k+1}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></p>
<table id="A10.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A10.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{encode}(d_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">encode</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{encode}(d_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E73.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\texttt{addr}_{d_{k+1}}\quad\text{(address matches AO-MDM's next decode position)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">addr</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(address matches AO-MDM’s next decode position)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\texttt{addr}_{d_{k+1}}\quad\text{(address matches AO-MDM's next decode position)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A10.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle z_{d_{k+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle z_{d_{k+1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A10.E74.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\texttt{tok}_{d_{k+1}}\quad\text{(token matches AO-MDM's next decode content)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tok</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(token matches AO-MDM’s next decode content)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\texttt{tok}_{d_{k+1}}\quad\text{(token matches AO-MDM's next decode content)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the position that AO-MDM will decode next, and <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{d_{k+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{d_{k+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the token that AO-MDM will generate at that position.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A10.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove this result, we decompose the architecture of the AO-MDM into two parts: the input transformation part (which can be represented as an operator <span id="A10.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">mdm_embed</span>) that transforms the token and position into an embedding, and the output generation part (which can be represented as an operator <span id="A10.p6.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">mdm_decode</span>) that transforms the embedding into logits, that is:</span></p>
<table id="A10.E75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A10.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{AO-MDM}(\mathbf{x})=\texttt{mdm\_decode}(\texttt{mdm\_embed}(\bar{\mathrm{TE}},\bar{\mathrm{PE}}))(\mathbf{x})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>AO-MDM</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">mdm_decode</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">mdm_embed</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>TE</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>PE</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AO-MDM}(\mathbf{x})=\texttt{mdm\_decode}(\texttt{mdm\_embed}(\bar{\mathrm{TE}},\bar{\mathrm{PE}}))(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A10.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A10.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathrm{TE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>TE</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathrm{TE}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A10.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathrm{PE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>PE</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathrm{PE}}</annotation></semantics></math> are seq-to-seq functions defined in <a href="#Thmdefinition5" title="Definition 5 (Canonical Extension to Seq-to-Seq Function). ‣ Appendix F Encoder Transformer Architecture ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">This decomposition is invariant to the choice of token and position embedding functions and AO-MDM’s parameter configuration. Simulating AO-MDM’s generation process boils down to the following two steps:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Replicating <span id="A10.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">mdm_embed</span>.<span id="A10.p8.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We construct initial layers of the Masked-ARM that, given the Masked-ARM state <math id="A10.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{\text{ARM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mtext>ARM</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{\text{ARM}}</annotation></semantics></math>, produce intermediate embeddings identical to <math id="A10.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{mdm\_embed}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">mdm_embed</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{mdm\_embed}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A10.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is the corresponding AO-MDM state. This transformation converts the address-token pair representation back into the embedding format that the AO-MDM expects, enabling the subsequent layers to perform identical computations.
We write the <span id="A10.p8.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> programs (which corresponds to the encoder Transformer construction) for the construction:</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A10.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<div id="A10.p9.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_python ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx111" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx111.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_comment ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">#<span id="lstnumberx111.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>----------------------<span id="lstnumberx111.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>Get<span id="lstnumberx111.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>logits<span id="lstnumberx111.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>identical<span id="lstnumberx111.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>to<span id="lstnumberx111.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>AO-MDM<span id="lstnumberx111.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>----------------------</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx112" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx112.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">mdm_logits</span><span id="lstnumberx112.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx112.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx112.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx112.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">mdm_decode</span><span id="lstnumberx112.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx112.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">embed_MDM</span><span id="lstnumberx112.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx113" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx113.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">tok_scores</span><span id="lstnumberx113.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx113.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx113.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx113.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">score</span><span id="lstnumberx113.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx113.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">mdm_logits</span><span id="lstnumberx113.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx114" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx115" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx115.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_comment ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">#<span id="lstnumberx115.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>AO-MDM<span id="lstnumberx115.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>candidate<span id="lstnumberx115.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>set:<span id="lstnumberx115.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>positions<span id="lstnumberx115.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>&gt;<span id="lstnumberx115.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>[SEP],<span id="lstnumberx115.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>still<span id="lstnumberx115.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>[MASK],<span id="lstnumberx115.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>and<span id="lstnumberx115.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>within<span id="lstnumberx115.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>valid<span id="lstnumberx115.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>range</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx116" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx116.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">cand_mask</span><span id="lstnumberx116.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx116.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx116.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx116.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx116.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">PE</span><span id="lstnumberx116.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx116.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&gt;</span><span id="lstnumberx116.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx116.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">sep_pos</span><span id="lstnumberx116.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span><span id="lstnumberx116.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx116.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">and</span><span id="lstnumberx116.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx116.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx116.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">TE</span><span id="lstnumberx116.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">_MDM</span><span id="lstnumberx116.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx116.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">==</span><span id="lstnumberx116.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx116.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">embed</span><span id="lstnumberx116.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">([</span><span id="lstnumberx116.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">MASK</span><span id="lstnumberx116.24" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">]))</span><span id="lstnumberx116.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx116.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">and</span><span id="lstnumberx116.27" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx116.28" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx116.29" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">PE</span><span id="lstnumberx116.30" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx116.31" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;=</span><span id="lstnumberx116.32" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx116.33" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">sn</span><span id="lstnumberx116.34" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx117" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx117.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">cand_score</span><span id="lstnumberx117.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx117.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx117.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx117.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx117.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">tok_scores</span><span id="lstnumberx117.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx117.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">if</span><span id="lstnumberx117.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx117.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">cand_mask</span><span id="lstnumberx117.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx117.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">else</span><span id="lstnumberx117.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx117.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">0)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx118" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx119" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx119.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">max_score</span><span id="lstnumberx119.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">  </span><span id="lstnumberx119.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx119.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx119.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph2 ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">seq_max</span><span id="lstnumberx119.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx119.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">cand_score</span><span id="lstnumberx119.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx120" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx120.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">is_best</span><span id="lstnumberx120.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">    </span><span id="lstnumberx120.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx120.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx120.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">cand_mask</span><span id="lstnumberx120.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx120.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">and</span><span id="lstnumberx120.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx120.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx120.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">tok_scores</span><span id="lstnumberx120.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx120.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">==</span><span id="lstnumberx120.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx120.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">max_score</span><span id="lstnumberx120.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx121" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx122" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx122.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_comment ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">#<span id="lstnumberx122.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>Select<span id="lstnumberx122.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>AO-MDM’s<span id="lstnumberx122.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>next<span id="lstnumberx122.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>decode<span id="lstnumberx122.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>position<span id="lstnumberx122.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>and<span id="lstnumberx122.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>corresponding<span id="lstnumberx122.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>logits</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx123" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx123.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">next_pos</span><span id="lstnumberx123.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">   </span><span id="lstnumberx123.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx123.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx123.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph2 ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">rightmost_exact_match</span><span id="lstnumberx123.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(1,</span><span id="lstnumberx123.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx123.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">is_best</span><span id="lstnumberx123.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx123.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx123.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">PE</span><span id="lstnumberx123.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx124" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx124.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">logits_next</span><span id="lstnumberx124.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx124.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx124.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx124.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph2 ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">rightmost_exact_match</span><span id="lstnumberx124.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx124.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">next_pos</span><span id="lstnumberx124.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx124.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx124.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">PE</span><span id="lstnumberx124.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx124.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx124.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">mdm_logits</span><span id="lstnumberx124.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx125" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx126" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx126.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_comment ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">#<span id="lstnumberx126.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>----------------------<span id="lstnumberx126.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>Emit<span id="lstnumberx126.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>as<span id="lstnumberx126.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>Masked-ARM<span id="lstnumberx126.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>&lt;addr,<span id="lstnumberx126.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>tok&gt;<span id="lstnumberx126.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>order<span id="lstnumberx126.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>----------------------</span>
</div>
