</div>
<div id="lstnumberx128" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx128.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">                                    </span><span id="lstnumberx128.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx128.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">PE</span><span id="lstnumberx128.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx128.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&gt;</span><span id="lstnumberx128.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx128.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">sep_pos</span><span id="lstnumberx128.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span><span id="lstnumberx128.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx128.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">and</span><span id="lstnumberx128.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx128.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx128.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">PE</span><span id="lstnumberx128.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx128.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;=</span><span id="lstnumberx128.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx128.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">sn</span><span id="lstnumberx128.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span><span id="lstnumberx128.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx128.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">and</span><span id="lstnumberx128.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx128.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx128.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">TE</span><span id="lstnumberx128.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx128.25" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">==</span><span id="lstnumberx128.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx128.27" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">embed</span><span id="lstnumberx128.28" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">([</span><span id="lstnumberx128.29" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">MASK</span><span id="lstnumberx128.30" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">])),</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx129" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx129.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">                                    </span><span id="lstnumberx129.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">PE</span><span id="lstnumberx129.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx130" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx130.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">emit_addr</span><span id="lstnumberx130.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx130.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx130.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx130.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(((</span><span id="lstnumberx130.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">gen_slot</span><span id="lstnumberx130.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx130.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">-</span><span id="lstnumberx130.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx130.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">sep_pos</span><span id="lstnumberx130.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)[:1])</span><span id="lstnumberx130.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx130.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">==</span><span id="lstnumberx130.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx130.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">0)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx131" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx132" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx132.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">if</span><span id="lstnumberx132.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx132.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">PE</span><span id="lstnumberx132.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx132.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">==</span><span id="lstnumberx132.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx132.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">gen_slot</span><span id="lstnumberx132.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx133" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx133.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">    </span><span id="lstnumberx133.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">result</span><span id="lstnumberx133.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx133.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx133.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx133.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx133.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">next_pos</span><span id="lstnumberx133.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx133.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">if</span><span id="lstnumberx133.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx133.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">emit_addr</span><span id="lstnumberx133.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx133.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">else</span><span id="lstnumberx133.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx133.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">logits_next</span><span id="lstnumberx133.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx134" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx134.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">else</span><span id="lstnumberx134.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx135" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx135.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">    </span><span id="lstnumberx135.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">result</span><span id="lstnumberx135.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx135.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx135.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx135.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">0</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx136" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx137" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx137.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">return</span><span id="lstnumberx137.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx137.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">result</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A10.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A10.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A10.p11.1" class="ltx_p">We remark the proof relies on two assumptions: 1) the function <math id="A10.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{S}(\mathbf{x})=S(|\mathbf{x}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{S}(\mathbf{x})=S(|\mathbf{x}|)</annotation></semantics></math> is deterministic and computable by encoder Transformer (this is implemented by the <span id="A10.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">sn</span> function in the <span id="A10.p11.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program for Step 1); 2) the confidence score is also dertermistic and computable by encoder Transformer (this is implemented by the <span id="A10.p11.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">score</span> operator in the <span id="A10.p11.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program for Step 2).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A11" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix K </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (AP-MDM Simulation of PRAM, Informal). ‣ 5.1 Universally Efficient Computation ‣ 5 The Power of Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h2>

<div id="Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 10</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(AP-MDM Simulation of PRAM, Formal)<span id="Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=(I_{0},\dots,I_{\ell},\mathrm{addr})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>addr</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=(I_{0},\dots,I_{\ell},\mathrm{addr})</annotation></semantics></math> be a uniform PRAM program with a finite instruction set of size <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, identical across processors and input size <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. On an initial memory state specified by address–value pairs <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{addr}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{val}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>addr</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{addr}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{val}})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{val}}\in\mathbb{U}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{val}}\in\mathbb{U}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{addr}}\in\mathcal{A}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>addr</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{addr}}\in\mathcal{A}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, suppose <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> runs in parallel time <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(n)</annotation></semantics></math> using at most <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)</annotation></semantics></math> processors and at most <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(n)</annotation></semantics></math> shared-memory words of <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math> bits, and outputs <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PRAM}_{\mathcal{P}}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{addr}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{val}})\in\mathbb{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>PRAM</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>addr</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕌</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PRAM}_{\mathcal{P}}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{addr}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{val}})\in\mathbb{U}</annotation></semantics></math> (see <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Parallel Random Access Machine ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>). Then there exists a bijection <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathbb{U}\cup\mathcal{A}\rightarrow\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕌</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathbb{U}\cup\mathcal{A}\rightarrow\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and an AP-MDM which, on input</span></p>
<table id="A11.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A11.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{x}=(z_{0},z_{1},\ldots,z_{n})\in\Sigma^{n+1},\quad z_{0}=\phi(P(n)),\;z_{i}=\phi(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{val},i})\text{ for }i=1,\ldots,n," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>val</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> for </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=(z_{0},z_{1},\ldots,z_{n})\in\Sigma^{n+1},\quad z_{0}=\phi(P(n)),\;z_{i}=\phi(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{val},i})\text{ for }i=1,\ldots,n,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">padded to context length <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(S(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(S(n))</annotation></semantics></math> (addresses provided implicitly by positional encodings), produces <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\!\left(\mathrm{PRAM}_{\mathcal{P}}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{addr}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{val}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.426em;" width="0.426em"><mi>ϕ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>PRAM</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>addr</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>val</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\!\left(\mathrm{PRAM}_{\mathcal{P}}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{addr}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{val}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T(n))</annotation></semantics></math> decoding steps.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first show that AP-MDM can simulate a weaker model called Rewrite-MDM, which is sufficient for the result. Then we construct an <span id="A11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program that simulates PRAM execution in a space-efficient manner.</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rewrite-MDM</span> follows the same framework as AP-MDM but with simplified control signals. For any token <math id="A11.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, define:</p>
<table id="A11.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A11.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{0.06,0.46,1}\textbf{remask}}_{x_{t,i},c_{t,i}}(y)=\begin{cases}y&amp;\text{if }c_{t,i}[1]=1\\
x_{t,i}&amp;\text{if }c_{t,i}[1]=0\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#0F75FF;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#0F75FF">remask</mtext><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>y</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\color[rgb]{0.06,0.46,1}\textbf{remask}}_{x_{t,i},c_{t,i}}(y)=\begin{cases}y&amp;\text{if }c_{t,i}[1]=1\\
x_{t,i}&amp;\text{if }c_{t,i}[1]=0\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A11.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A11.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t,i}[1]\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t,i}[1]\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a binary rewrite signal. In other words, when <math id="A11.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t,i}[1]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t,i}[1]=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the model rewrites position <math id="A11.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with new content <math id="A11.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>; when <math id="A11.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t,i}[1]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t,i}[1]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, it preserves the original content <math id="A11.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> unchanged.</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We next show how each transition <math id="A11.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}\rightarrow\mathbf{z}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}\rightarrow\mathbf{z}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> in Rewrite-MDM can be simulated by exactly three steps of AP-MDM as defined in <a href="#S4" title="4 Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 11</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(AP-MDM Simulation of Rewrite-MDM)<span id="Thmtheorem11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any Rewrite-MDM transition <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}\rightarrow\mathbf{z}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}\rightarrow\mathbf{z}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> on sequence of length <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a sequence of three AP-MDM steps that produces the identical result.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A11.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A11.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given a Rewrite-MDM transition where we want to selectively rewrite positions in sequence <math id="A11.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}=(z_{t,1},z_{t,2},\ldots,z_{t,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}=(z_{t,1},z_{t,2},\ldots,z_{t,n})</annotation></semantics></math> according to rewrite signal <math id="A11.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{t}=(r_{t,1},r_{t,2},\ldots,r_{t,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{t}=(r_{t,1},r_{t,2},\ldots,r_{t,n})</annotation></semantics></math>, we simulate this using the following three AP-MDM steps: <math id="A11.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}\rightarrow\mathbf{u}^{(1)}\rightarrow\mathbf{u}^{(2)}\rightarrow\mathbf{u}^{(3)}=\mathbf{z}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}\rightarrow\mathbf{u}^{(1)}\rightarrow\mathbf{u}^{(2)}\rightarrow\mathbf{u}^{(3)}=\mathbf{z}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1 (Insert):<span id="A11.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Starting from <math id="A11.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, apply <span id="A11.p5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFB529;">insert</span> operation at every position <math id="A11.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> to create an expanded sequence of length <math id="A11.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A11.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A11.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{u}^{(1)}=(g\circ f_{\theta})(\mathbf{z}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{u}^{(1)}=(g\circ f_{\theta})(\mathbf{z}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A11.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A11.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(1)}_{i}[1]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(1)}_{i}[1]=0</annotation></semantics></math> (no remask), <math id="A11.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(1)}_{i}[2]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(1)}_{i}[2]=1</annotation></semantics></math> (insert), <math id="A11.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(1)}_{i}[3]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(1)}_{i}[3]=0</annotation></semantics></math> (no delete) for all <math id="A11.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>.
This yields <math id="A11.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}^{(1)}=(z_{t,1},\textsf{M},z_{t,2},\textsf{M},\ldots,z_{t,n},\textsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}^{(1)}=(z_{t,1},\textsf{M},z_{t,2},\textsf{M},\ldots,z_{t,n},\textsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2 (Unmask and Remask):<span id="A11.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Apply AP-MDM’s <math id="A11.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g\circ f_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g\circ f_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> operation on <math id="A11.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> with control signals:</span></span></p>
<table id="A11.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A11.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{u}^{(2)}=(g\circ f_{\theta})(\mathbf{u}^{(1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{u}^{(2)}=(g\circ f_{\theta})(\mathbf{u}^{(1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A11.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the control signals are set as follows:</span></p>
<ul id="A11.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A11.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A11.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For even positions <math id="A11.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2i</annotation></semantics></math> (newly inserted masks): <math id="A11.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(2)}_{2i}[1]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(2)}_{2i}[1]=0</annotation></semantics></math> (unmask), <math id="A11.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(2)}_{2i}[2]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(2)}_{2i}[2]=0</annotation></semantics></math> (no insert), <math id="A11.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(2)}_{2i}[3]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(2)}_{2i}[3]=0</annotation></semantics></math> (no delete)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A11.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A11.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For odd positions <math id="A11.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2i-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2i-1</annotation></semantics></math> (original tokens): <math id="A11.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(2)}_{2i-1}[1]=r_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(2)}_{2i-1}[1]=r_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> (remask), <math id="A11.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(2)}_{2i-1}[2]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(2)}_{2i-1}[2]=0</annotation></semantics></math> (no insert), <math id="A11.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(2)}_{2i-1}[3]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(2)}_{2i-1}[3]=0</annotation></semantics></math> (no delete)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A11.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">which yield <math id="A11.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}^{(2)}=(\textsf{M},z_{t+1,1},\textsf{M},z_{t+1,2},\ldots,\textsf{M},z_{t+1,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}^{(2)}=(\textsf{M},z_{t+1,1},\textsf{M},z_{t+1,2},\ldots,\textsf{M},z_{t+1,n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3 (Delete):<span id="A11.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Apply AP-MDM’s <math id="A11.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g\circ f_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g\circ f_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> operation again to <span id="A11.p7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B80000;">delete</span> all mask tokens at original positions:</span></span></p>
<table id="A11.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A11.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{u}^{(3)}=(g\circ f_{\theta})(\mathbf{u}^{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{u}^{(3)}=(g\circ f_{\theta})(\mathbf{u}^{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A11.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where for all positions <math id="A11.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A11.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}^{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}^{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ul id="A11.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A11.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A11.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For odd positions <math id="A11.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2i-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2i-1</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A11.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(3)}_{2i-1}[1]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(3)}_{2i-1}[1]=0</annotation></semantics></math> (no remask), <math id="A11.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(3)}_{2i-1}[2]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(3)}_{2i-1}[2]=0</annotation></semantics></math> (no insert), <math id="A11.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c^{(3)}_{2i-1}[3]=\mathds{1}[u^{(2)}_{2i-1}=\textsf{M}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(3)}_{2i-1}[3]=\mathds{1}[u^{(2)}_{2i-1}=\textsf{M}]</annotation></semantics></math> (delete if mask)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A11.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A11.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For even positions <math id="A11.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2i</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A11.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(3)}_{2i}[1]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(3)}_{2i}[1]=0</annotation></semantics></math> (no remask), <math id="A11.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(3)}_{2i}[2]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(3)}_{2i}[2]=0</annotation></semantics></math> (no insert), <math id="A11.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{(3)}_{2i}[3]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{(3)}_{2i}[3]=0</annotation></semantics></math> (no delete)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A11.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">This removes all mask tokens at odd positions and recovers the original length <math id="A11.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. By construction, <math id="A11.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}^{(3)}=\mathbf{z}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}^{(3)}=\mathbf{z}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the simulation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State Tracking Mechanism<span id="A11.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">    To enable the AP-MDM to autonomously determine which of the three simulation steps to execute, we augment sequences with special boundary tokens <span id="A11.p8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">[BOS]</span> and <span id="A11.p8.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">[EOS]</span>. The model identifies the current phase by examining the boundary token configuration:</span></span></p>
<ul id="A11.I3" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A11.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A11.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1 (Insert):</span> Normal state with <span id="A11.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">[BOS]</span> at the beginning and <span id="A11.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">[EOS]</span> at the end</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A11.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A11.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2 (Unmask and Remask):</span> <span id="A11.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">[EOS]</span> is followed by a <span id="A11.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">M</span> token, indicating expanded state</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A11.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A11.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3 (Delete):</span> <span id="A11.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">[BOS]</span> is preceded by a <span id="A11.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_sansserif">M</span> token, signaling cleanup phase</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A11.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">During Step 2, the model leverages the first bit of positional encodings (e.g. <span id="A11.p8.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">BiPE</span> introduced in <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Key Tool: Encoder Full-Access Sequence Processing (E-FASP) ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>) to distinguish between original positions (odd indices) and newly inserted positions (even indices), enabling it to correctly apply remasking operations to original positions based on the rewrite signal <math id="A11.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> while unmasking new positions to write content from <math id="A11.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A11.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We omit the Transformer-based construction for the procedure described above for brevity, which can be done by a simple <span id="A11.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A11.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We use the Rewrite-MDM variant established above to simulate PRAM algorithms with optimal space complexity. Here we use the <math id="A11.p10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{BiPE};[\cdot]_{+},\times]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">E-FASP</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">BiPE</mtext><mo>;</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">×</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{E-FASP}[\texttt{BiPE};[\cdot]_{+},\times]</annotation></semantics></math> variant with binary positional encoding (<a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Key Tool: Encoder Full-Access Sequence Processing (E-FASP) ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>). The input that encodes the PRAM’s initial memory state is a sequence <math id="A11.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n+1})\in\Sigma^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n+1})\in\Sigma^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> of discrete tokens from the vocabulary <math id="A11.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A11.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A11.E80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E80.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\in\Sigma\quad\text{(processor count token)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>(processor count token)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\Sigma\quad\text{(processor count token)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A11.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E81.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\in\Sigma\quad\text{(data token)}\quad\text{for }i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>(data token)</mtext><mtext>for </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\Sigma\quad\text{(data token)}\quad\text{for }i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A11.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Through token embedding <math id="A11.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TE}:\Sigma\to\mathbb{R}^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TE}:\Sigma\to\mathbb{R}^{w}</annotation></semantics></math>, these discrete tokens are mapped to their semantic bit representations:</p>
<table id="A11.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A11.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{TE}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{TE}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mapsto P(n)\in\{0,1\}^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mapsto P(n)\in\{0,1\}^{w}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A11.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{TE}(x_{i+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{TE}(x_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E83.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mapsto\text{val}_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{w}\quad\text{(data bits)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mtext>val</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi></msup><mtext>(data bits)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mapsto\text{val}_{i}\in\{0,1\}^{w}\quad\text{(data bits)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A11.p11.2" class="ltx_p">for <math id="A11.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>. The actual input to the AP-MDM is the padded sequence <math id="A11.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}=(x_{0,1},x_{0,2},\ldots,x_{0,S(n)})\in\bar{\Sigma}^{S(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}=(x_{0,1},x_{0,2},\ldots,x_{0,S(n)})\in\bar{\Sigma}^{S(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A11.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Sigma}=\Sigma\cup\{\textsf{M}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Sigma}=\Sigma\cup\{\textsf{M}\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A11.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A11.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{0,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{0,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E84.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{j}\quad\text{for }j=1,\ldots,n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mtext>for </mtext><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{j}\quad\text{for }j=1,\ldots,n+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A11.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{0,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{0,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E85.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\textsf{M}\quad\text{for }j=n+2,\ldots,S(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mtext>for </mtext><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\textsf{M}\quad\text{for }j=n+2,\ldots,S(n)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A11.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p12.1" class="ltx_p">The crucial advantage of AP-MDM is that it can dynamically rewrite the content at any position using the <span id="A11.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0F75FF;">remask</span> operation, allowing the simulation to use space optimally as <math id="A11.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(S(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(S(n))</annotation></semantics></math> rather than the <math id="A11.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(P(n)\times T(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(P(n)\times T(n))</annotation></semantics></math> required by standard MDM.</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p13.1" class="ltx_p">We next provide an overview of the construction:</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p14.1" class="ltx_p">The key difference between how Rewrite-MDM and AO-MDM simulate PRAM is that Rewrite-MDM can directly rewrite the memory at any position and each computation does not necessarily has be kept in the context forever. This enables us to get rid of the address token. Now representation of a processor can be simplified to:</p>
<table id="A11.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A11.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A11.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ldots\langle\texttt{PC}_{1},\texttt{R}_{1,1},\texttt{R}_{1,2},\texttt{R}_{1,3}\rangle\;\langle\texttt{PC}_{2},\texttt{R}_{2,1},\texttt{R}_{2,2},\texttt{R}_{2,3}\rangle\;\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">PC</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">PC</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">R</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ldots\langle\texttt{PC}_{1},\texttt{R}_{1,1},\texttt{R}_{1,2},\texttt{R}_{1,3}\rangle\;\langle\texttt{PC}_{2},\texttt{R}_{2,1},\texttt{R}_{2,2},\texttt{R}_{2,3}\rangle\;\ldots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A11.p14.2" class="ltx_p">where we only use 3 registers (this is sufficient for the proof but can be extended to any <math id="A11.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.p15.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, we do not append processor representations to the end of input <math id="A11.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> as in AO-MDM, but instead will initialize them at the end of the entire sequence. The remaining part of the sequence is used as a shared memory where token embeddings are data and positional encodings are addresses, aligning more closely with PRAM.</p>
</div>
<section id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Intialization.</h5>

<div id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When the last position is a mask token, we initialize the processor state and computation log at the end of the sequence. Roles of each token are calculated similarly as the construction in AO-MDM (except it is static throughout the generation process).</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The execution of the program is similar to the construction in AO-MDM, except now the address is inherently associated with the positional encoding. The termination is also slightly different: the returned embedding has to contain an additional bit to indicate the rewrite operation. Also, the termination condition is no longer when all masked are unmasked but a flexibly defined one: in our case, when all processors are HALT.</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using the operators defined above, we now construct an <span id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program that simulates PRAM execution. The program implements the single-processor algorithm detailed in <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Parallel Random Access Machine ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<div id="A11.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_python ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx138" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx138.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_comment ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">#<span id="lstnumberx138.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>----------------------<span id="lstnumberx138.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>Roles<span id="lstnumberx138.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>&amp;<span id="lstnumberx138.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>Layout<span id="lstnumberx138.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">  </span>----------------------</span>
</div>
