<div id="lstnumberx233" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx233.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">    </span><span id="lstnumberx233.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">val</span><span id="lstnumberx233.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx233.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx233.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx233.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_emph2 ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">rightmost_exact_match</span><span id="lstnumberx233.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx233.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">PE</span><span id="lstnumberx233.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx233.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx233.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">STORE_KEYS</span><span id="lstnumberx233.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx233.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx233.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">STORE_VALS</span><span id="lstnumberx233.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx233.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx233.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">TE</span><span id="lstnumberx233.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx234" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx235" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx235.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">    </span><span id="lstnumberx235.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_comment ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">#<span id="lstnumberx235.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>all<span id="lstnumberx235.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>halt:<span id="lstnumberx235.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>do<span id="lstnumberx235.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>not<span id="lstnumberx235.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>rewrite;<span id="lstnumberx235.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>otherwise,<span id="lstnumberx235.2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>if<span id="lstnumberx235.2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>hit,<span id="lstnumberx235.2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>rewrite<span id="lstnumberx235.2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>this<span id="lstnumberx235.2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>address<span id="lstnumberx235.2.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>(even<span id="lstnumberx235.2.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>if<span id="lstnumberx235.2.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>not<span id="lstnumberx235.2.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>MASK<span id="lstnumberx235.2.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>originally)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx236" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx236.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">    </span><span id="lstnumberx236.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">if</span><span id="lstnumberx236.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx236.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">hit</span><span id="lstnumberx236.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx236.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">==</span><span id="lstnumberx236.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx236.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">1:</span><span id="lstnumberx236.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx236.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">return</span><span id="lstnumberx236.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx236.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx236.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">val</span><span id="lstnumberx236.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx236.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx236.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">1)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx237" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx237.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">    </span><span id="lstnumberx237.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_keyword ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">else</span><span id="lstnumberx237.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">:</span><span id="lstnumberx237.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">        </span><span id="lstnumberx237.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">return</span><span id="lstnumberx237.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx237.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx237.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">TE</span><span id="lstnumberx237.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx237.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx237.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">0)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx238" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx239" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx239.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">return</span><span id="lstnumberx239.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx239.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx239.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_literate ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;">TE</span><span id="lstnumberx239.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx239.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx239.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">0)</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A12" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix L </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Generating Two-Sided Dyck-𝑘, Informal). ‣ 5.2 Structural Generation: Examples in Coding and Science ‣ 5 The Power of Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h2>

<div id="Thmdefinition11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 11</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Two-Sided Dyck-<math id="Thmdefinition11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmdefinition11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{k}=\{a_{1}^{\pm 1},\dots,a_{k}^{\pm 1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{k}=\{a_{1}^{\pm 1},\dots,a_{k}^{\pm 1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\Rightarrow v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\Rightarrow v</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained from <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> by deleting a factor <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}a_{i}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}a_{i}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{-1}a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{-1}a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,k\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Write <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u\Rightarrow^{*}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\Rightarrow^{*}v</annotation></semantics></math> iff there exist <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and words <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=w_{0},\dots,w_{m}=v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=w_{0},\dots,w_{m}=v</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{j}\Rightarrow w_{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{j}\Rightarrow w_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A12.E87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.E87.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}\;:=\;\{\,w\in\Sigma_{k}^{*}\;:\;w\Rightarrow^{*}\varepsilon\,\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>TDyck</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mi>w</mi><msup><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}\;:=\;\{\,w\in\Sigma_{k}^{*}\;:\;w\Rightarrow^{*}\varepsilon\,\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition11.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition11.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is the empty word.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the Two-Sided Dyck-<math id="A12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> language, we define the vocabulary as:</p>
<table id="A12.E88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\{a_{1}^{+1},a_{1}^{-1},a_{2}^{+1},a_{2}^{-1},\ldots,a_{k}^{+1},a_{k}^{-1}\}\cup\{\texttt{[BOS]},\texttt{[EOS]}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[BOS]</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[EOS]</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\{a_{1}^{+1},a_{1}^{-1},a_{2}^{+1},a_{2}^{-1},\ldots,a_{k}^{+1},a_{k}^{-1}\}\cup\{\texttt{[BOS]},\texttt{[EOS]}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A12.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the extended vocabulary <math id="A12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Sigma}=\Sigma\cup\{\textsf{M}_{1},\textsf{M}_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Sigma}=\Sigma\cup\{\textsf{M}_{1},\textsf{M}_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{i}^{\pm 1}\}_{i=1}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{i}^{\pm 1}\}_{i=1}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are the <math id="A12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2k</annotation></semantics></math> bracket tokens, <span id="A12.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">[BOS]</span> and <span id="A12.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">[EOS]</span> are boundary tokens, and <math id="A12.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{1},\textsf{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{1},\textsf{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are two types of mask tokens used to handle an inherent limitation of vanilla masked diffusion when extended to the non-deterministic case (i.e. given two mask tokens, the model can not randomly generate <math id="A12.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AA</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A12.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BB</annotation></semantics></math> without also having probability to generate <math id="A12.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A12.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BA</annotation></semantics></math>). Thus <math id="A12.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Sigma|=2k+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Sigma|=2k+2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A12.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\bar{\Sigma}|=2k+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\bar{\Sigma}|=2k+4</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A12.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Merrill et al., 2022</a>)</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 12</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Hardmax)<span id="Thmdefinition12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmdefinition12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the zero-temperature softmax (Hardmax) as</span></p>
<table id="A12.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{softmax}_{0}(x)\;\triangleq\;\lim_{\tau\to 0^{+}}\mathrm{softmax}_{\tau}(x),\quad\text{where}\quad[\mathrm{softmax}_{0}(x)]_{i}=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{|\arg\max_{j}x_{j}|},&amp;i\in\arg\max_{j}x_{j},\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{softmax}_{0}(x)\;\triangleq\;\lim_{\tau\to 0^{+}}\mathrm{softmax}_{\tau}(x),\quad\text{where}\quad[\mathrm{softmax}_{0}(x)]_{i}=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{|\arg\max_{j}x_{j}|},&amp;i\in\arg\max_{j}x_{j},\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 13</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stochastic AP-MDM)<span id="Thmdefinition13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A stochastic AP-MDM is defined as an AP-MDM with encoder-only Transformer backbone as in <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Encoder Transformer Architecture ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>, where instead of greedy decoding, we use sampling from Hardmax distributions. Formally, let <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Enc}_{\theta}:\Sigma^{*}\to(\mathbb{R}^{d})^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Enc</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Enc}_{\theta}:\Sigma^{*}\to(\mathbb{R}^{d})^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be the encoder Transformer (before the final projection layer) as defined in <a href="#Thmdefinition7" title="Definition 7 (Encoder Transformer). ‣ Residual Connections. ‣ Appendix F Encoder Transformer Architecture ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. For each position <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in the input sequence, let <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}_{i}=[\mathrm{Enc}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x})]_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Enc</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}_{i}=[\mathrm{Enc}_{\theta}(\mathbf{x})]_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the hidden state. Define logits <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(v\mid\mathbf{x},i)=\langle\mathbf{h}_{i},\mathrm{TE}(v)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(v\mid\mathbf{x},i)=\langle\mathbf{h}_{i},\mathrm{TE}(v)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and the probability distribution over vocabulary <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> as:</span></p>
<table id="A12.E89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A12.E89.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(v\mid\mathbf{x},i)=[\mathrm{softmax}_{0}(\ell(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x},i))]_{v}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(v\mid\mathbf{x},i)=[\mathrm{softmax}_{0}(\ell(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x},i))]_{v}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition13.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition13.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{softmax}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>softmax</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{softmax}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Hardmax function from <a href="#Thmdefinition12" title="Definition 12 (Hardmax). ‣ Appendix L Proof of ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>. The stochastic AP-MDM samples tokens according to <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v_{i}\sim\text{Categorical}(p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x},i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Categorical</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}\sim\text{Categorical}(p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x},i))</annotation></semantics></math>. For the insert operation to support two types of mask tokens (<math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>), we use two separate classification heads <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PROJ}_{I_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>PROJ</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PROJ}_{I_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PROJ}_{I_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>PROJ</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PROJ}_{I_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> whose outputs are thresholded for inserting <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, with priority: <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> takes precedence over <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We disable remask and delete operations for this construction.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 12</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Generating Two-Sided Dyck-<math id="Thmtheorem12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, Formal)<span id="Thmtheorem12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a stochastic AP-MDM as in <a href="#Thmdefinition13" title="Definition 13 (Stochastic AP-MDM). ‣ Appendix L Proof of ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> with constant-depth Transformer backbone such that the support of the induced distribution of AP-MDM over strings <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly equal to <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>TDyck</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, that is,</span></p>
<ol id="A12.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:10pt;">
<li id="A12.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A12.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><em id="A12.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">Coverage</em><span id="A12.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) For every </span><math id="A12.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>TDyck</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A12.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A12.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr_{\theta}[w]&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr_{\theta}[w]&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A12.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A12.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A12.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><em id="A12.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">Support exactness</em><span id="A12.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) For every </span><math id="A12.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\notin\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>TDyck</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\notin\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A12.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A12.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr_{\theta}[w]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr_{\theta}[w]=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A12.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem12.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Conversely, under the common hardness assumption that <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{TC}^{0}\neq\textsf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">TC</mtext><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">NC</mtext><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{TC}^{0}\neq\textsf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any constant-depth ARM with polylogarithmic embedding dimension, there exists <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the support of the distribution generated ARM cannot be exactly equal to <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>TDyck</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A12.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A12.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the claim about ARM, we will prove by contradiction. First we note that every <math id="A12.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\Sigma_{k}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\Sigma_{k}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a <math id="A12.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}\in\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>TDyck</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}\in\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A12.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is a prefix of <math id="A12.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. (The existence of such <math id="A12.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is straightforward, for example, one can construct it by taking <math id="A12.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}=ww^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}=ww^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the inverse is performed by viewing <math id="A12.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> as an element of the corresponding free group) Now we suppose ARM can indeed generate a distribution whose support is exactly equal to <math id="A12.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>TDyck</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This implies that the ARM must be able to determine at each generation step whether the current sequence can be terminated. Specifically, the model must assess whether the currently generated sequence satisfies the complete bracket matching condition. If the sequence is properly matched, the probability of outputting <span id="A12.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">[EOS]</span> must be non-zero to enable termination. Therefore, the difficulty of generating matched brackets reduces to the problem of recognizing whether a given sequence forms valid matched brackets. For the two-sided Dyck-<math id="A12.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> language, this recognition problem is DLOGTIME-uniform <math id="A12.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">NC</mtext><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-hard <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Robinson, 1993</a>)</cite>, which exceeds the computational capacity of constant-depth Transformers which is in <math id="A12.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{TC}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">TC</mtext><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{TC}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, under the hardness assumption that <math id="A12.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{TC}^{0}\neq\textsf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">TC</mtext><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">NC</mtext><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{TC}^{0}\neq\textsf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus we conclude ARM cannot generate a distribution over <math id="A12.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{k}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{k}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> whose support is exactly equal to <math id="A12.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>TDyck</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A12.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the stochastic AP-MDM, we construct the following algorithm to generate all strings in the two-sided Dyck-<math id="A12.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> language through the following algorithmic procedure, illustrated in <a href="#S1.F2.sf2" title="In Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(b)</span></a>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A12.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1 (Probabilistic Mask Insertion):<span id="A12.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> If the current sequence contains no mask tokens, then for any sequence position <math id="A12.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> not containing an end-of-sequence token, the model inserts <math id="A12.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with constant probability <math id="A12.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> using the insert operation from <a href="#S4" title="4 Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. The insertion probability for <math id="A12.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is set to zero at this stage.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A12.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2 (Uniform Token Selection):<span id="A12.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> At positions containing <math id="A12.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the model performs two operations: (i) it samples uniformly from the bracket token set <math id="A12.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{i}^{\pm 1}\}_{i=1}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{i}^{\pm 1}\}_{i=1}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> to determine the content, and (ii) it inserts <math id="A12.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability 1. Due to the priority-based insertion mechanism defined in <a href="#Thmdefinition13" title="Definition 13 (Stochastic AP-MDM). ‣ Appendix L Proof of ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, <math id="A12.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> overrides <math id="A12.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, making the original insertion probability irrelevant for subsequent processing.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A12.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3 (Context-Aware Bracket Matching):<span id="A12.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> When processing <math id="A12.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, the model identifies the nearest bracket token <math id="A12.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}^{\pm 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}^{\pm 1}</annotation></semantics></math> to the left of the current position and generates the corresponding matching bracket according to the two-sided Dyck-<math id="A12.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> reduction rules.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A12.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Termination Condition:<span id="A12.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The termination mechanism operates as follows: In Step 2, when the sequence contains <math id="A12.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> tokens but no <math id="A12.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, the model inserts <math id="A12.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> at the final position with a fixed probability. Subsequently, in Step 3, when processing this final <math id="A12.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> token, the model generates <span id="A12.p8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">[EOS]</span> (given the binary positional encoding we considered in <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Parallel Random Access Machine ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>, the model is able to identify if the token should be decoded as <span id="A12.p8.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">[EOS]</span> or a matching bracket), signaling the end of the generation process.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A12.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The above algorithm admits an <span id="A12.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program implementation (see <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Key Tool: Encoder Full-Access Sequence Processing (E-FASP) ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>) with the following treatment of stochastic operations:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A12.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">For uniform sampling over the <math id="A12.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2k</annotation></semantics></math> bracket tokens, we exploit the fixed vocabulary size by assigning each bracket token <math id="A12.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{\pm 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{\pm 1}</annotation></semantics></math> to distinct dimensions in the <math id="A12.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional embedding space. Specifically, when the <span id="A12.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program needs to output a uniform distribution over a subset <math id="A12.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq\{a_{i}^{\pm 1}\}_{i=1}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq\{a_{i}^{\pm 1}\}_{i=1}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, it returns a hidden state <math id="A12.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A12.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{h},\mathrm{TE}(v)\rangle=c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{h},\mathrm{TE}(v)\rangle=c</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A12.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in S</annotation></semantics></math> (for some constant <math id="A12.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="A12.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{h},\mathrm{TE}(v^{\prime})\rangle&lt;c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>TE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{h},\mathrm{TE}(v^{\prime})\rangle&lt;c</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A12.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\prime}\notin S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\prime}\notin S</annotation></semantics></math>. The hardmax from <a href="#Thmdefinition13" title="Definition 13 (Stochastic AP-MDM). ‣ Appendix L Proof of ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, ensures that the probability mass concentrates uniformly over <math id="A12.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, achieving the desired uniform sampling behavior.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A12.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A12.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is easy to see that this generation procedure can produce any string in the two-sided Dyck-<math id="A12.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> language, and since any token that would violate Dyck constraints always has strictly smaller logit and hence probability <math id="A12.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> under Hardmax, the support of the distribution is exactly <math id="A12.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>TDyck</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TDyck}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A12.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A12.p12.1" class="ltx_p">We note the introduction of two mask tokens is for the model to distinguish between different steps, but this is not necessary if we allow some random seeds in input which mitigates the limitation of MDM when extending to the non-deterministic case.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A13" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix M </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (Hardness of Simulating AP-MDM, Informal). ‣ 5.4 Hardness of Being Simulated ‣ 5 The Power of Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h2>

<section id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Edit Triplet Encoding.</h5>

<div id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We encode each elementary edit as a triplet of tokens <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\texttt{op},\,\texttt{pos},\,\texttt{val}\rangle\in\Sigma_{\mathrm{op}}\times\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}\times\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">op</mtext><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">pos</mtext><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">val</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>pos</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\texttt{op},\,\texttt{pos},\,\texttt{val}\rangle\in\Sigma_{\mathrm{op}}\times\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}\times\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, where</p>
<table id="A13.E90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\mathrm{op}}=\{\texttt{UNMASK},\texttt{INSERT},\texttt{DELETE},\texttt{REMASK}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">UNMASK</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">INSERT</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">DELETE</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">REMASK</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\mathrm{op}}=\{\texttt{UNMASK},\texttt{INSERT},\texttt{DELETE},\texttt{REMASK}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The position token set <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>pos</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}</annotation></semantics></math> reuses the earlier address/position encoding in <a href="#Thmdefinition10" title="Definition 10 (Position/Content Tokens and Address Encoding). ‣ Appendix J Proof of ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>: a position <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[S(n)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[S(n)]</annotation></semantics></math> is encoded as <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{pos}=\texttt{encode}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">pos</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">encode</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{pos}=\texttt{encode}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> with inverse decoding <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{dec\_pos}(\texttt{pos})=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">dec_pos</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">pos</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{dec\_pos}(\texttt{pos})=i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The semantics of the triplet follows the instantiation of AP-MDM considered in <a href="#S4" title="4 Any-Process Generation ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">
          
            §
          
        </span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 14</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Editing Sequence)<span id="Thmdefinition14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition14.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given an input sequence <math id="Thmdefinition14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\bar{\Sigma}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\bar{\Sigma}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, an editing sequence is a finite sequence of triplets</span></p>
<table id="A13.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A13.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A13.E91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T(\mathbf{x})=\big(\langle\mathrm{op}_{j},\,\mathrm{pos}_{j},\,\mathrm{val}_{j}\rangle\big)_{j=1}^{m(\mathbf{x})},\quad\mathrm{op}_{j}\in\Sigma_{\mathrm{op}},\;\mathrm{pos}_{j}\in\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}},\;\mathrm{val}_{j}\in\Sigma." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>op</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>pos</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>val</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>op</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>op</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>pos</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>pos</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>val</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T(\mathbf{x})=\big(\langle\mathrm{op}_{j},\,\mathrm{pos}_{j},\,\mathrm{val}_{j}\rangle\big)_{j=1}^{m(\mathbf{x})},\quad\mathrm{op}_{j}\in\Sigma_{\mathrm{op}},\;\mathrm{pos}_{j}\in\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}},\;\mathrm{val}_{j}\in\Sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition14.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition14.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition14.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Its application to <math id="Thmdefinition14.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined recursively by <math id="Thmdefinition14.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{(0)}=\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{(0)}=\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A13.E92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.E92.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{(j)}=\mathrm{Apply}\big(\langle\mathrm{op}_{j},\mathrm{pos}_{j},\mathrm{val}_{j}\rangle,\,\mathbf{x}^{(j-1)}\big),\quad j=1,\ldots,m(\mathbf{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>Apply</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>op</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>pos</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>val</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{(j)}=\mathrm{Apply}\big(\langle\mathrm{op}_{j},\mathrm{pos}_{j},\mathrm{val}_{j}\rangle,\,\mathbf{x}^{(j-1)}\big),\quad j=1,\ldots,m(\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition14.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition14.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We write</span></p>
<table id="A13.E93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Apply\_Triplets}\big(T(\mathbf{x}),\,\mathbf{x}\big):=\mathbf{x}^{(m(\mathbf{x}))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Apply</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Triplets</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Apply\_Triplets}\big(T(\mathbf{x}),\,\mathbf{x}\big):=\mathbf{x}^{(m(\mathbf{x}))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition14.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition14.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">An editing sequence is valid iff every intermediate application is well-defined under the triplet semantics (e.g., <span id="Thmdefinition14.p2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">UNMASK</span> applies only to masks).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 13</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Hardness of Simulating AP-MDM, Formal)<span id="Thmtheorem13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists an AP-MDM <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> with a constant-depth encoder-only Transformer backbone such that no ARM or Masked-ARM <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 3 (Masked-ARM). ‣ 3.3 (Limited) Power of Any-Order Generation ‣ 3 A Theory of Masked Diffusion ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) with a constant-depth decoder-only Transformer backbone can, on every input <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, produce an editing sequence <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{G}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{G}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#Thmdefinition14" title="Definition 14 (Editing Sequence). ‣ Edit Triplet Encoding. ‣ Appendix M Proof of ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) that realizes <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>’s generation process; i.e., under the assumption that constant-depth Transformers do not include <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsf{TC}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">TC</mtext><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsf{TC}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A13.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall G\;\exists\,\mathbf{x}\in\bar{\Sigma}^{*}:\;\mathrm{Apply\_Triplets}\big(T_{G}(\mathbf{x}),\,\mathbf{x}\big)\;\neq\;\mathrm{Apply\_Triplets}\big(T_{F}(\mathbf{x}),\,\mathbf{x}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∃</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Apply</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Triplets</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≠</mo><mrow><mi>Apply</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Triplets</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall G\;\exists\,\mathbf{x}\in\bar{\Sigma}^{*}:\;\mathrm{Apply\_Triplets}\big(T_{G}(\mathbf{x}),\,\mathbf{x}\big)\;\neq\;\mathrm{Apply\_Triplets}\big(T_{F}(\mathbf{x}),\,\mathbf{x}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">or <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{G}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{G}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> is invalid.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The ARM in the above result can be replaced by the Masked-ARM with encoder architecture used in <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Left-to-Right v.s. Any-Order, Informal). ‣ 3.3 (Limited) Power of Any-Order Generation ‣ 3 A Theory of Masked Diffusion ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> without affecting the result.</p>
</div>
<div id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}\in\Sigma^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}\in\Sigma^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be the base string, let <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> be a valid editing sequence (<a href="#Thmdefinition14" title="Definition 14 (Editing Sequence). ‣ Edit Triplet Encoding. ‣ Appendix M Proof of ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), and let <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>pos</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\Sigma_{\mathrm{pos}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a query position token with index <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=\mathrm{dec\_pos}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>dec</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>pos</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=\mathrm{dec\_pos}(q)</annotation></semantics></math>. Encode the input as</span></p>
<table id="A13.E94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}=(\mathbf{u},\;\texttt{[SEP]},\;\mathrm{flatten}(T),\;\texttt{[SEP]},\;q,\;\texttt{[SEP]})\in\Sigma^{L+3+3m(\mathbf{u})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[SEP]</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>flatten</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[SEP]</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[SEP]</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=(\mathbf{u},\;\texttt{[SEP]},\;\mathrm{flatten}(T),\;\texttt{[SEP]},\;q,\;\texttt{[SEP]})\in\Sigma^{L+3+3m(\mathbf{u})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here</span></p>
<table id="A13.E95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.E95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{flatten}(T)=(\mathrm{op}_{1},\mathrm{pos}_{1},\mathrm{val}_{1},\ldots,\mathrm{op}_{m},\mathrm{pos}_{m},\mathrm{val}_{m})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>flatten</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>op</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>pos</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>val</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>op</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>pos</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>val</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{flatten}(T)=(\mathrm{op}_{1},\mathrm{pos}_{1},\mathrm{val}_{1},\ldots,\mathrm{op}_{m},\mathrm{pos}_{m},\mathrm{val}_{m}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">The task is to output the queried symbol after applying the editing history:</span></p>
<table id="A13.E96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\;=\;\big[\mathrm{Apply\_Triplets}\big(T(\mathbf{u}),\,\mathbf{u}\big)\big]_{i}\;\in\;\Sigma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>Apply</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Triplets</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\;=\;\big[\mathrm{Apply\_Triplets}\big(T(\mathbf{u}),\,\mathbf{u}\big)\big]_{i}\;\in\;\Sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">That is, the instance provides (i) a base string <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, (ii) an editing history <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> as a sequence of triplets, and (iii) a query position token <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. The model must simulate <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and return the symbol at the queried position <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in the resulting string. For AP-MDM, the simulation is intuitive and can be proven by simple <span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">E-FASP</span> program which we skip in this proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For ARM, due to the construction of the problem, the simulation process
is exactly copying the editing sequence part in the input, therefore
solving the problem is equivalent to directly answer the query, which we
show the equivalence to a <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TC}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖳𝖢</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TC}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-hard task:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmdefinition15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Preserves</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Allender et al., 2006</a>)</cite>)<span id="Thmdefinition15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition15.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be an ordered list (1-indexed). The update alphabet is</span></p>
<table id="A13.E97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.E97.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{U}=\{\texttt{insert}(i),\,\texttt{delete}(i)\mid i\in\mathbb{N}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">insert</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">delete</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}=\{\texttt{insert}(i),\,\texttt{delete}(i)\mid i\in\mathbb{N}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(97)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition15.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition15.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For an initial list <math id="Thmdefinition15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and an update sequence <math id="Thmdefinition15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{U}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{U}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmdefinition15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the list after applying the first <math id="Thmdefinition15.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> updates of <math id="Thmdefinition15.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.
For indices <math id="Thmdefinition15.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A13.E98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.E98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PRESERVES}(A_{0},s,i,j)\iff\text{the item at position }i\text{ in }A_{0}\text{ still exists after }s\text{ and is at position }j\text{ in }A_{|s|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>PRESERVES</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">the item at position </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> in </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> still exists after </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and is at position </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> in </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PRESERVES}(A_{0},s,i,j)\iff\text{the item at position }i\text{ in }A_{0}\text{ still exists after }s\text{ and is at position }j\text{ in }A_{|s|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition15.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition15.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The decision problem <span id="Thmdefinition15.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Preserves</span> asks, given <math id="Thmdefinition15.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{0},s,i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{0},s,i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>, whether <math id="Thmdefinition15.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PRESERVES}(A_{0},s,i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>PRESERVES</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PRESERVES}(A_{0},s,i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> holds.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_conjecture">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conjecture 14</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The <span id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Preserves</span> problem is <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖭𝖢</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-hard under DLOGTIME-uniform reductions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We reduce <span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Preserves</span> to our Editing-Query task in one step. Given <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{0},s,i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{0},s,i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A_{0}|=L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{0}|=L</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}\in\Sigma^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}\in\Sigma^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> list the items of <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (unique token id per item); expand each <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{insert}(p,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">insert</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{insert}(p,v)</annotation></semantics></math> as the triplet block <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\langle\texttt{INSERT},\mathrm{encode}(p),\textsf{M}\rangle,\langle\texttt{UNMASK},\mathrm{encode}(p^{\prime}),v\rangle\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">INSERT</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>encode</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">UNMASK</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>encode</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\langle\texttt{INSERT},\mathrm{encode}(p),\textsf{M}\rangle,\langle\texttt{UNMASK},\mathrm{encode}(p^{\prime}),v\rangle\big)</annotation></semantics></math> and each <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{delete}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">delete</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{delete}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\big(\langle\texttt{REMASK},\mathrm{encode}(p),\bullet\rangle,\langle\texttt{DELETE},\mathrm{encode}(p),\bullet\rangle\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">REMASK</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>encode</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">DELETE</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>encode</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\langle\texttt{REMASK},\mathrm{encode}(p),\bullet\rangle,\langle\texttt{DELETE},\mathrm{encode}(p),\bullet\rangle\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the position of the newly inserted mask under our convention and <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math> is ignored; let <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> be the concatenation over <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=\mathrm{encode}(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>encode</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=\mathrm{encode}(j)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then with</span></p>
<table id="A13.E99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\;=\;\big[\mathrm{Apply\_Triplets}\big(T,\mathbf{u}\big)\big]_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>Apply</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Triplets</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\;=\;\big[\mathrm{Apply\_Triplets}\big(T,\mathbf{u}\big)\big]_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">we have</span></p>
<table id="A13.E100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A13.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PRESERVES}(A_{0},s,i,j)\;\Longleftrightarrow\;y=\mathrm{id}(i)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>PRESERVES</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>id</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PRESERVES}(A_{0},s,i,j)\;\Longleftrightarrow\;y=\mathrm{id}(i).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus any model that solves Editing-Query on all inputs also decides <span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Preserves</span>. By <a href="#Thmtheorem14" title="Conjecture 14. ‣ Proof. ‣ Edit Triplet Encoding. ‣ Appendix M Proof of ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Conjecture</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, <span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Preserves</span> is <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖭𝖢</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-hard, which places it beyond the computational capacity of constant-depth Transformers that are contained in <math id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{TC}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖳𝖢</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{TC}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this conjecture, no constant-depth ARM or Masked-ARM can solve our Editing-Query task on all inputs. This completes the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A13.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A14" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix N </span>Experiment: Sudoku Puzzle</h2>

<div id="A14.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A14.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide detailed description of training data generation for the Sudoku puzzle experiment. The data generation process simulates a backtracking-based solving algorithm and records the intermediate states as supervised training trajectories for AP-MDM.</p>
</div>
<section id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">State Representation</h5>

<div id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9\times 9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9\times 9</annotation></semantics></math> Sudoku grid is represented as a sequence of 324 tokens, where each cell is encoded using 3 consecutive tokens: <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{value},\text{color},\text{marker})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>value</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>color</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>marker</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{value},\text{color},\text{marker})</annotation></semantics></math>. The vocabulary consists of 32 tokens including: EMPTY (unfilled cell), MASK (unknown position to be predicted), digits 1-9 (filled values), WHITE (default color indicating no branch), 15 branch COLOR tokens (tracking different branching paths), NORMAL (standard state), SKULL (failed branch point), BRANCH (active branch starting position), and SEPARATOR (structural delimiter between cells). The value token can be EMPTY (for unfilled cells), a digit 1-9 (for filled cells), or MASK (for positions being predicted). The color token tracks which branching decision path the cell belongs to, using WHITE for non-branched cells and one of 15 COLOR tokens for cells within branches. The marker token indicates the cell’s computational status: NORMAL for standard cells, SKULL for positions that caused backtracking, and BRANCH for branch starting points.</p>
</div>
<div id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The solving algorithm consists of several atomic operations, each translated into state-transition tuples for AP-MDM training:</p>
</div>
<div id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assign and Branch:</span> The two most fundamental operations in Sudoku solving are deterministic assignment and branch creation, both implemented through combinations of <span id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0F75FF;">remask</span> and <span id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9933CC;">unmask</span> operations. For Assign, when deterministically filling a cell with value <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, we generate a 2-step transition: first, the three tokens at the target position are remasked, converting them to <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\textsf{M},\textsf{M},\textsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\textsf{M},\textsf{M},\textsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math>; second, these masks are unmasked to the target values <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v,c,\text{NORMAL})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>NORMAL</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v,c,\text{NORMAL})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is the appropriate color token determined by the current branch context. For Branch, when creating a branch at position <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r,c)</annotation></semantics></math> with candidate value <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and branch identifier <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, we similarly generate a 2-step transition: first, remask the cell tokens to <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\textsf{M},\textsf{M},\textsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\textsf{M},\textsf{M},\textsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math>; second, unmask to <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v,\text{COLOR}_{b},\text{BRANCH})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext>COLOR</mtext><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext>BRANCH</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v,\text{COLOR}_{b},\text{BRANCH})</annotation></semantics></math> to mark this cell as a branch starting point with the corresponding branch color.</p>
</div>
<div id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Concrete examples visualizing these two operations are shown in <a href="#A14.F5" title="In Training Data Statistics ‣ Appendix N Experiment: Sudoku Puzzle ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Contradiction Marking, Backtrack, and Recovery:</span> When the solver detects a contradiction (a cell with no valid candidates), before backtracking, we mark this contradicting position through a 2-step transition: first remask the cell to <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\textsf{M},\textsf{M},\textsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\textsf{M},\textsf{M},\textsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, then unmask to <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{EMPTY},\text{COLOR}_{b},\text{SKULL})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>EMPTY</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext>COLOR</mtext><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext>SKULL</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{EMPTY},\text{COLOR}_{b},\text{SKULL})</annotation></semantics></math> to visually indicate the contradiction location. When backtracking from a failed branch, multiple cells need to be cleared through a 2-step transition that handles both ordinary cells and the branch starting point differently: in the first step, ordinary cells are remasked in all three token positions while the branch starting point only has its marker token remasked; in the second step, ordinary cells are unmasked to <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{EMPTY},\text{WHITE},\text{NORMAL})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>EMPTY</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>WHITE</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>NORMAL</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{EMPTY},\text{WHITE},\text{NORMAL})</annotation></semantics></math> while the branch starting point undergoes simultaneous remask and unmask operations with the first two positions remasked to <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\textsf{M},\textsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\textsf{M},\textsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math> and the third position unmasked to store the failed value. After backtracking, when filling the failed position with a new value, we generate a 2-step transition to convert from the SKULL state: the first step unmasks the value and color while remasking the marker to <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\textsf{M},\textsf{M},v_{\text{old}})\to(v_{\text{new}},c,\textsf{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">M</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\textsf{M},\textsf{M},v_{\text{old}})\to(v_{\text{new}},c,\textsf{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second step unmasks the marker to either NORMAL or BRANCH depending on whether this creates a new branch. Concrete examples visualizing these operations are shown in <a href="#A14.F6" title="In Training Data Statistics ‣ Appendix N Experiment: Sudoku Puzzle ‣ On Powerful Ways to Generate: Autoregression, Diffusion, and Beyond" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training Data Statistics</h5>

<div id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following this generation process, each Sudoku puzzle produces 1421.3 state-transition tuples (i.e. from <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A14.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>) on average depending on the puzzle difficulty and the number of backtracking steps required. For our experiments, we generated training data from 100 hard Sudoku puzzles, each yielding 25,022.6 training state-transition tuples on average.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A14.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
